urity\": 9,\n        \"validation\": 9,\n        \"overall\": 9\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\nSCOPE NONFILES {\n  \"chunk_instruction\": \"docs/planning/chunks/C29.md\",\n  \"specification\": \"docs/architecture/ui-v2/ (reviewed in C27, commit c0ac8b30)\",\n  \"excluded_unrelated_user_work\": \"Modified paths not listed in scope belong to the owner's in-progress C26 attempt-02 and academy-2.1 work (see git status) and are out of scope.\",\n  \"removed_since_prior_request\": [],\n  \"standing_generation\": \"current integrated tree after C44 and L19 correction; no fabricated predecessor completion\"\n}\nEVIDENCE ENVELOPE []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat GLOSSARY.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/invariants.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/state-ownership.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/wizard.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat GLOSSARY.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/invariants.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/state-ownership.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/wizard.md'","aggregated_output":"# Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 domain vocabulary\n\nThese terms name the desktop product and its native authority concepts.\nMechanisms, wire formats and transition rules belong in the selected design.\n\n## Language\n\n**Tenant profile**: An application-owned configuration for a Prisma AIRS tenant,\nincluding its label, endpoints, and protected credential references. A scan-only\nprofile does not require management OAuth credentials. A profile is not an\nAcademy learner account or a Gateway workspace.\n\n**Credential capability**: The specific operations a credential can authorize,\nsuch as scanning, management, inference, or workspace MCP. Possessing one\ncapability does not establish another; configuration keeps them explicit.\n\n**Gateway workspace**: A remote AI Gateway administrative/inference context within\nthe selected tenant profile. It is distinct from a local filesystem project.\n\n**Configuration review**: An operator-visible proposal for an AIRS configuration\nchange, bound to the current tenant, credential context, target resource, and\ndraft. Rust owns its validity. Displaying or importing a proposal does not grant\npermission to apply it.\n\n**Remote outcome**: What is known about an attempted remote action: not sent,\nrejected, completed as established by evidence, or unknown. Local timeout,\ncancellation, and disconnection do not establish remote rollback.\n\n**Academy feature**: The learner experience within the broader desktop app.\nPresentation is shared with Academy; remote learning contracts remain hosted.\nLearning progression, XP, cosmetic credits, awards, and other gamification stay\nwithin this feature.\n\n**Academy learner account**: The remote learning identity owning progress,\nassessments, certificates, and account-scoped local drafts/downloads. It is\nindependent of the selected Prisma AIRS tenant and Harness inference sign-in.\n\n**Shared presentation**: React controls, themes, and shell layout reused from the\nAcademy-owned source. Sharing appearance does not share learner authority,\ngamification effects, manager routes, or browser-session assumptions globally.\n\n**Harness**: The assistant feature using the native Rust agent engine and\ndesktop-owned lifecycle, credential grants, reviews, and protected history.\nThe SCM SDK is a separate dependency, not the Harness engine.\n\n**Project scope**: The explicitly selected local filesystem scope and approved\ntool permissions available to a Harness conversation. Preserve the existing\nrestrictions initially; a transcript is not permission to restore approvals.\n\n**MCP grant**: A desktop-owned authorization context for a specific remote MCP\nbinding. Inference sign-in is separate. Discovery does not establish execution;\nexecution evidence must correspond to the actual approved call.\n\n**Historical conversation**: Saved user work that can be inspected after import.\nResumption requires separate context/protocol compatibility validation. It never\nrestores pending approvals or old authentication sessions.\n\n**Billing**: Desktop commercial charging/monetization machinery, excluded from\nv2. Remote Gateway usage/cost/budget/limit administration remains product\nfunctionality. Academy's earned learning economy remains Academy-local.\n\n**Shipped backend runtime**: Executables/workers required by the installed app's\nbackend. Node/Bun and TypeScript backend workers are excluded. Build-time JS\ntooling and React JavaScript executing in the WebView are separate concepts.\n\n**Parity**: Coverage of agreed working v1 behavior with new v2 evidence. V1 source\nimplementation, retained fixture/contract results, retained live evidence, and\nv2 installed-artifact results are distinct. Replacing a preview/stub with a live\nfeature is scope expansion, not implicit parity work.\n\n**Authority principal**: The native-established operator or restricted Harness\nidentity on whose behalf desktop work is requested. A claimed identity in a\nrequest is not an Authority principal.\n\n**Authority handle**: A principal-scoped entry to native desktop operations and\nobservations. Possessing an operation reference does not expand its authority.\n\n**Intent**: A typed request for a specific desktop action under the caller's\ncurrent authority. It is distinct from a Harness proposal or an arbitrary remote\nrequest.\n\n**Receipt**: Native acknowledgement that an Intent was admitted, with its request\nor operation reference. It is not evidence of operator confirmation or remote\ncompletion.\n\n**Refusal**: Native rejection of an Intent before admission under the requested\nauthority. A remote action's failure is a Remote outcome instead.\n\n**ViewScope**: The product context a caller asks to observe, such as a learner\naccount, tenant workspace or Harness conversation. Native authority determines\nwhich part is visible to that caller.\n\n**Observation**: A scoped redacted view of native desktop state and operation\nprogress. It confers no execution or credential authority.\n\n**ContextRef**: A native reference to the particular product context presented\nto the caller. Returning to the same tenant or account does not revive retired\nauthority.\n\n**Delivery session**: The current native-registered channel for one caller's\nIntent deliveries. It is separate from tenant, learner or inference identity.\n\n**Delivery sequence**: The order identity of an Intent within its Delivery session,\nused to distinguish duplicate delivery from an explicit new action.\n_Avoid_: Business retry, authorization token\n\n**Native-owned payload reference**: A scoped reference to staged desktop input\nwhose ownership and content are known natively. It is not permission to read an\narbitrary filesystem path.\n\n**Reviewed**: A Configuration review whose captured proposal remains eligible for\noperator confirmation.\n\n**Confirming**: A Configuration review currently awaiting the native operator's\nanswer for that specific proposal.\n\n**Consumed**: A Configuration review already committed to its single admitted\noperation. Failure of that operation does not make the review reusable.\n\n**Queued**: An admitted desktop operation whose remote dispatch has not been\nclaimed.\n\n**DispatchClaimed**: A desktop operation for which remote dispatch may have begun.\nLocal cancellation at this stage does not prove NotSent.\n\n**Settled**: A desktop operation with a recorded terminal local result and its\ncurrent Remote outcome. Later reconciliation may refine knowledge of that outcome.\n\n**Harness grant**: Native authority for one verified inference identity and its\napproved tenant/workspace/origin context. Rotating that identity's token material\nis distinct from replacing or revoking the Harness grant.\n\n**Grant epoch**: The particular lifetime of a native grant's authority. Retired\nauthority stays retired even when an equivalent identity is selected again.\n\n**One-time secret receipt**: The operator-scoped acknowledgement holding newly\nissued secret material for its explicit transient reveal. It is separate from a\nstored credential lookup.\n\n**Editor lease**: The hold on the reviewed document while native operator\nconfirmation is pending. A changed document or context invalidates that hold.\n# UI v2 \"Refined Native\" — design specification\n\nStatus: C27 deliverable, reviewed at the 9/10 bar (D058). This document and\nits companions ([tokens](tokens.md), [state ownership](state-ownership.md),\n[invariants](invariants.md), [screens](screens/), [provenance](provenance.md))\nare what every P09 chunk is judged against. The existing\n[DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md) remains authoritative for the native authority\ninterface, transport, Academy presentation ownership and the Harness; this\ndocument changes only how the desktop presents those.\n\n## 1. Scope and deliverable\n\nThe reviewed prototype is extracted in three layers, in order:\n\n1. **Spec** (C27, this folder): tokens, screen inventory, state ownership,\n   invariants, interaction contracts, copy, provenance, acceptance criteria.\n2. **TypeScript presentation** (C28–C29, then per-destination chunks): the new\n   shell and screens in `apps/desktop`, built against wire fixtures and the\n   mock runtime, behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag.\n3. **Rust contract** (within each destination chunk): the intents, scopes and\n   refusals the screens need, implemented over existing desktop-core services\n   and exported through ts-rs.\n\nThe first implementation slice is the shell plus the first-run wizard and\nadd-tenant sheet (C28–C29). Harness, Inbox/reads, reviews/Administration, API\nClient, Test Cases and the Academy embed follow (C30–C34). The legacy shell,\nits feature-view switch, the flag and the legacy native acceptance scripts are\nremoved in C34; the phase is not complete while any destination renders only\nin the legacy shell.\n\n## 2. Frozen reference\n\nCanvas https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL, page \"Refined Native\nv2\", version 134. The six R2 files are copied verbatim under\n[prototype/](prototype/) with SHA-256 hashes in `MANIFEST.sha256`. They are\nimmutable inputs. Codex scored the prototype 8/10 on rounds 4–16; the five\nopen round-16 items are carried as known gaps (§10) and closed in\nimplementation, not by further prototype rounds.\n\n## 3. Architecture fit\n\n- **Authority** stays with desktop-core (D014). The UI dispatches intents and\n  observes scopes through the existing two-command Tauri bridge. Every\n  prototype state field is assigned in [state-ownership.md](state-ownership.md);\n  no persisted or tenant-sensitive state is UI-owned (UI state is transient\n  presentation state only), and no state goes to browser storage.\n- **Contract**: new intents, scopes and refusals are Rust types with ts-rs\n  derives, regenerated by `xtask bindings`. A hand-written parser is added to\n  the contracts client only where runtime validation beyond the type is needed.\n- **Shell flag**: `ShellSnapshot.ui_variant` (`legacy` | `v2`) and\n  `ShellSnapshot.onboarding` (`needed` | `inProgress` | `done`) are Rust-owned,\n  fixture-able and seedable by native acceptance. The React root switches on\n  them.\n- **Navigation inventory**: one Rust list (feature ids with availability,\n  label, shortcut index and sidebar membership) feeds the native menu, the\n  sidebar and the command palette. Feature ids gain `home` and `inbox`;\n  `library` is shown as \"Test Cases\"; `gateway` and `redTeam` render inside\n  Administration's accordion; `sessions`, `import` and `settings` stay\n  reachable from the palette and Administration.\n- **Shortcuts** ⌘1–⌘9 are defined by the native menu, which dispatches\n  `navigate`; the sidebar displays the menu's truth.\n- **Transient state**: a small zustand store per screen family (shell, wizard,\n  inbox, admin, harness, workbench); React state only for form fields.\n- **Tokens**: local `--v2-*` custom properties ([tokens.md](tokens.md));\n  Academy variables untouched for the embedded learner view.\n- **Copy**: one `copy.ts` per screen family exporting constants; tests assert\n  exact strings. The voice is the wizard's: this app is built entirely on\n  Palo Alto Networks' public APIs and exists to show application builders what\n  those interfaces make possible; it explains the API call as you go.\n- **Show the calls**: a Rust-owned preference reveals, for each action, the\n  request and response as the diagnostics module already redacts them\n  (credential ids in place of secrets, a note that the core attaches the real\n  header). Default on until onboarding completes.\n\n## 4. Layout rhythm\n\nShared by every destination, the wizard and the add-tenant sheet:\n\n- 32px top and 44px side page margins; 26px/700 titles; 18–20px card\n  padding; 10–12px gaps; 32px controls; 14px body, 12px secondary (11px only\n  pills, eyebrows and mono badges); 860px reading cap; 244px rail (first-run\n  wizard rail 320px).\n- Minimum window 1180×720. Below 1280 wide the rail collapses to icons with\n  tooltips; nothing scrolls horizontally.\n- Tool workspaces (Harness, API Client) have a title row like every other\n  destination; no destination is exempt from the rhythm.\n\n## 5. Destinations\n\n| Sidebar | Feature id | Shortcut | Contract |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Home | `home` (new) | ⌘1 | [screens/shell.md](screens/shell.md) |\n| Inbox | `inbox` (new) | ⌘2 | [screens/inbox-reads.md](screens/inbox-reads.md) |\n| Harness | `harness` | ⌘3 | [screens/harness.md](screens/harness.md) |\n| Academy | `academy` | ⌘4 | [screens/academy.md](screens/academy.md) |\n| Test Cases | `library` | ⌘5 | [screens/api-client-test-cases.md](screens/api-client-test-cases.md) |\n| API Client | `apiClient` | ⌘6 | same |\n| Administration | `administration` (+ `gateway`, `redTeam` inside) | ⌘7 | [screens/reviews-administration.md](screens/reviews-administration.md) |\n| Tenant switcher | — | ⌘T | [screens/shell.md](screens/shell.md) |\n| Command palette | — | ⌘K | same |\n| First-run wizard, add-tenant sheet | — | — | [screens/wizard.md](screens/wizard.md) |\n\nRed Team is read-only everywhere. Gamification appears only inside the Academy\nembed. Product availability is governed by §6.\n\n## 6. Products, admitted services and the unsupported boundary\n\nThe prototype shows six products. Only a product with an admitted service in\ndesktop-core is verified, inventoried or changed; the rest render as\nunavailable. Nothing in P09 adds a product API.\n\n| Product | Admitted reads | Admitted changes | P09 treatment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AI Runtime Security | `ManagementResource` (profiles, topics, applications, API keys, deployment profiles, DLP catalog/profiles/patterns, filtering profiles, dictionaries, sessions); scan (`scan.rs`) | `ChangeKind` Profiles, Topics, Applications, ApiKeys, DataPatterns, DataProfiles, FilteringProfiles, Dictionaries with `ChangeAction` Create/Version/Rotate/Delete/… (`changes.rs`) | Full: Administration tabs, reviews, Playground, Inbox items |\n| AI Gateway | `GatewayRead` (inventory, detail, integration models, prerequisites, observe, MCP servers) | Gateway `ChangeKind`s (workspaces, providers, routes, guardrails, service/user keys, integrations) | Full, inside Administration; Harness lifecycle 2 reads `McpServers` |\n| AI Red Teaming | `red_team.rs` reads (scan inventory, statistics, static reports; C13) | none (execution stays a disabled preview) | Read-only card and tabs; Test Cases \"Inspect\" only |\n| Model/skill observability (AI Supply Chain in the prototype) | C13 model/skill reads | none | Read-only; shown under its C13 name, never as a scanning product |\n| Agentic Identity Security | none | none | **Not available in this release**: card and accordion entry with the dependency gate (\"needs an admitted AIS service; see D058\"); not selectable in the wizard; never verified; no inventory, no policy review |\n| Agentic Endpoint Security | none | none | Same as AIS; the prototype's AES policy review, discovered-AI table and warning demo are fixtures only and are not implemented |\n\nThe per-tab and per-action mapping, including the restricted Runtime and\nGateway change matrices (for example no application Create, no API-key\nUpdate, no data-profile Delete) and every removed or unavailable prototype\ntab, is enumerated in\n[screens/administration-inventory.md](screens/administration-inventory.md).\n\nRules: an unavailable product or tab never produces a verification result, an\nInbox item, an inventory row or a review. The wizard's verify step lists it\nas \"Not available\" (not pass, warning or fail). Test V2-T19 asserts that the\nadmin inventory for an unavailable product has no tabs and no actions, and\nV2-R10 asserts that no intent exists that would mutate it; V2-T20 and V2-R11\ncover unavailable tabs and denied actions within admitted products.\n\n## 7. Error presentation\n\n- **Refusal** (core refused an intent): warn toast with the refusal reason and\n  the tenant named; never a modal. Guard-type refusals (tenant switch with a\n  pending decision) render their dialog from the refusal payload.\n- **Delivery unknown**: inline \"not confirmed\" state on the control that\n  dispatched, with Retry; the control is not reset.\n- **Contract violation**: generic warn toast; detail to diagnostics.\n\n## 8. Accessibility additions\n\nThe native acceptance checklist gains four items that every P09 chunk's\nacceptance script asserts: accent-colour focus ring on every focusable\ncontrol (inset variant where declared); `role=\"status\"` live regions for read\nstatus, API send completion and review apply; one topmost modal with\n`aria-hidden` siblings and focus return; toasts persist under Reduce Motion.\nExisting requirements (keyboard-only, VoiceOver attributes, 150%/200% zoom,\ncontrast AA) continue to apply to every changed screen.\n\n## 9. Budgets\n\nExisting `budgets.json` entries carry unchanged. New: a tenant switch renders\nthe new tenant's Home from cached scopes within 100 ms, with read status\nshowing pending until the read lands (measured by the C30 workload).\n\n## 10. Known gaps carried from the prototype\n\nCodex round 16 (score 8) left five items, closed by the chunk named:\n\n1. Secret disclosure survives a tenant switch with the key review open → I6, C31.\n2. Applied injection-override examples show \"Not demonstrated\" → topic\n   verdicts keyed separately from detectors, profile-aware, C31.\n3. Administration creation labels from a per-product single value → per-tab\n   `AdminInventory` capability and label, C31.\n4. Home snooze tooltip hard-codes \"Snooze 24 hours\" → shared item\n   `snoozeLabel`, I11, C30.\n5. API Client Send announces nothing → `role=\"status\"` completion region, C33.\n\n## 11. Verification\n\n- Behaviour: Vitest + Testing Library component tests, one named fixture per\n  prototype wrapper board; the board → initial props → test id table is in\n  [screens/boards.md](screens/boards.md), so reviewed-state coverage can be\n  audited without reconstructing canvas wrappers.\n- Contract: Rust integration tests per invariant (`V2-Rxx`).\n- Native: the existing Accessibility-API scripts, extended per chunk, plus a\n  screenshot evidence set per chunk at 100% and 200% zoom in both themes filed\n  under `evidence/Cxx/screens/`.\n- Live: only C29 (wizard verify against Vulture, reads only) and C31 (review\n  apply against Redtail under the `airs-v2-c25-` prefix) run live, inside the\n  scope the owner designated on 2026-10-25. Every other chunk runs on fixtures\n  and the mock runtime.\n- Review: C27 at 9/10 in every dimension, enforced by the controller (a\n  `docs_only` chunk refuses owner acceptance and needs no native\n  preparation); C28–C34 may complete at 8 under D034 and are raised to 9\n  before the P09 phase review.\n- Legacy native scripts removed in C34 are first mapped, assertion by\n  assertion, to replacement native-check ids (C34 milestone 2), so the\n  cumulative P09 gate keeps exercising every earlier authority and\n  accessibility requirement.\n# Normative invariants\n\nThese twelve rules are the behaviours Codex forced into the prototype over\nsixteen review rounds. They are normative: an implementation chunk that\nviolates one fails its behaviour or authority dimension regardless of how the\nscreen looks. Code shape is free; the rule and its test are not.\n\nEach rule names its acceptance test id. `V2-Txx` tests are Vitest component\ntests in the desktop app (fixture-driven); `V2-Rxx` are Rust integration tests\nin desktop-core; `V2-Nxx` are native acceptance checks added to\n`native-checks.json` by the chunk that implements the rule.\n\n| Id | Rule | Tests | Chunk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | There is exactly one tenant-switch path. The core refuses a switch while a Harness decision is pending; the UI renders the archive-or-discard guard from the refusal and re-dispatches with the chosen resolution. | V2-R01 refusal on pending decision; V2-T01 guard rendered from refusal payload; V2-N01 switch via switcher, palette and menu all pass through the guard | C30 |\n| I2 | Every observed scope is per tenant. Switching tenants never shows another tenant's Inbox items, reads, reviews, conversations, drafts or rotation state. | V2-R02 scope isolation across two tenants; V2-T02 switcher round-trip leaves per-tenant transient state intact | C30 |\n| I3 | A review is bound to the tenant and resource it was opened for and applies only when the typed name matches, validated in the core. A tenant change invalidates the review. | V2-R03 confirmReview refuses on mismatch and on changed context; V2-T03 Apply disabled until names match | C31 |\n| I4 | Reads are finite. The UI distinguishes \"first read pending\" from \"no activity\", reports per-product partial coverage, and the completion toast is warn-kind whenever any source is partial. | V2-R04 ReadStatus transitions; V2-T04 toast kind and text per coverage; V2-N02 pending state visible on first run | C30 |\n| I5 | API responses are immutable snapshots. A later configuration change never alters an earlier response in history; a newly sent request reflects the change. | V2-R05 history entries hash-stable; V2-T05 topic applied → old response unchanged, new response includes it | C33 |\n| I6 | An issued secret is disclosed only through the host (`RevealSecret` sheet, host clipboard), is held per result for the active context and never persisted; any review exit, including a tenant switch or context retirement, drops it (`ForgetSecret`) and resets the reveal state. A dropped secret is not recoverable; the UI offers to issue another key. | V2-R06 held key dropped on review exit, switch and retirement; Reveal after drop refuses; V2-T06 resumed rotation shows no secret controls | C31 |\n| I7 | Key rotation is the admitted sequence additional key (`Version`) → local deployment acknowledgement → old key `Delete` with readback. Until the old key is removed, the reminder is a distinct Inbox item with its own identity and stated return time and the key table shows both keys. Two timestamps are stored once and labelled distinctly: deployment acknowledged (local statement) and old key removed (remote readback). A failed or unknown issuance never reissues automatically; a rejected or unknown Delete keeps the reminder and leaves the completion timestamp unset; unknown outcomes are shown as unconfirmed with reconciliation, never as complete. | V2-R07 state machine incl. failed/unknown issuance and rejected/unknown delete; V2-T07 Inbox item lifecycle; V2-T08 timestamps labelled and stable after refresh | C31 |\n| I8 | One topmost modal. Siblings of the topmost dialog are `aria-hidden`; Escape closes only the topmost; focus returns to the opener. | V2-T09 stacking; V2-N03 keyboard-only dialog traversal | C28 |\n| I9 | A verdict or severity is colour plus icon plus word, never colour alone. | V2-T10 every verdict renderer emits all three; V2-N04 accessibility tree carries the word | C28 |\n| I10 | Toasts have a kind (ok, info, warn), expire on a timer, and are presentation only: everything a toast says is derivable from an observed scope. With Reduce Motion on, toasts persist until dismissed. | V2-T11 kinds and expiry; V2-N05 Reduce Motion persistence | C28 |\n| I11 | Inbox acknowledge and snooze are per item, core-owned, with the return time stated wherever the action is offered (Home, Inbox row, Inbox detail) and identical across them. | V2-R08 snooze return computed in core; V2-T12 Home and Inbox labels equal | C30 |\n| I12 | A fresh tenant never shows seeded or sample data. Its first Harness send creates a user conversation; its Inbox is empty until the first read lands. | V2-R09 fresh tenant scopes empty; V2-T13 first send creates conversation | C30, C32 |\n\nRules I1, I3, I6 and I7 are authority rules under D014: the core owns the\ndecision, the UI renders it. No invariant may be satisfied by invented data: a\nproduct, tab or operation without an admitted service renders as unavailable\n(DESIGN-V2 §6), and a test that passes only on fixtures for such a capability\nis a specification defect.\n# State ownership\n\nEvery state key the frozen prototype actually holds is listed here, by file\nand by the name the prototype uses, with its owner, where it lives, its\nlifetime, and whether the implementation keeps, renames, derives or drops it.\n\n- **Core** — Rust-owned in desktop-core, exposed through `observe`\n  (persisted in the store or session-held), never in browser storage.\n- **UI** — transient presentation state in a per-screen-family zustand store\n  (shell, wizard, inbox, admin, harness, workbench) or React form state.\n  Lost on reload by design.\n- **Host** — never leaves the native host (secret sheet, clipboard).\n- **Dropped** — not implemented; the reason is in [provenance.md](provenance.md).\n\nThe inventory was produced from `grep -o` over `s.*`, `ts.*` and `f.*` in\n`prototype/R2App.dc.html` and `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html` (version 134)\nand reconciled by hand; a key missing here is a specification defect.\n\n## R2Onboard — wizard and add-tenant sheet (`s.*`, `s.f.*`)\n\n| Prototype key | Meaning | Owner | Where / intent | Lifetime | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `s.idx`, `s.path`, `s.vi` | current step, step path, visited steps | UI | wizard store | until the wizard closes | kept; `onboarding=inProgress` is set in core when the welcome step is left |\n| `s.f.name` | tenant display name | UI → Core | `completeOnboarding`/`addTenant` | written at completion | kept |\n| `s.env`, `s.region` | environment, region selects | UI → Core | same | same | kept |\n| `s.f.tsg` | TSG id (10 digits) | UI → Core | same | same | kept |\n| `s.f.clientId`, `s.f.secret` | management OAuth client id and secret (required in the prototype) | id: UI → Core; secret: **Host** | id in `addTenant`; secret entered only in the host secret sheet, vault record id returned | secret never in the web layer | **changed** (deviation P17): management credentials become an optional second section under D013; the id is kept, the secret field is replaced by \"Add management client…\" |\n| `s.scanOn`, `s.f.scanKey` | scan key toggle and value | toggle: UI; key: **Host** | \"Add scan key…\" opens the host secret sheet; required for first run (D013) | never in the web layer | **changed** (P1, P17): toggle removed on first run (the scan key is required); kept in add mode |\n| `s.gwOn`, `s.f.ws`, `s.f.endpoint`, `s.f.gwKey` | Gateway section toggle, workspace name, endpoint URL, workspace key | toggle/ws/endpoint: UI → Core; key: **Host** | `addTenant.gateway{ws, endpoint}`; key via secret sheet | — | kept; key path changed (P1) |\n| `s.tried`, `s.vsig`, `s.vsStale` | validation attempted, validation signature, stale flag | UI (tried) / Core (signature, stale) | wizard component; `setup.verify.stale`, `setup.completable` | per step / per draft | kept; the signature and the completion gate moved to the core so the presentation cannot complete over stale results |\n| `s.vs` | verify results per product | Core | `ShellSnapshot.setup.verify` (streamed `VerifyStep`s from `verifyTenantSetup`, with `done`/`failed`/`stale`) | until the draft completes or is discarded | kept; computed in core, including staleness against a signature of the draft's inputs |\n| `s.aesFixed`, `s.failCleared` | AES warning demo acknowledged; failed row cleared | UI | wizard store | per run | **changed**: AES is not an admitted product (P18); the warning demo becomes a generic \"warning row\" fixture on an admitted product |\n| `s.prods` | selected products | UI → Core | `completeOnboarding.products` | written at completion | kept; unavailable products are not selectable (P18) |\n| `s.packs`, `s.casesState` | starter packs selected, pack state | UI → Core | `completeTenantSetup.products` → the bundled catalog's cases as library entries named by their starter pack, Not run (P55) | written at completion | kept |\n| `s.acad`, `s.af` (`f.email`, `f.dname`), `s.streaks`, `s.remind` | local Academy account form, streaks, reminders | **Dropped** / Core (Academy) | Academy identity is hosted (D004–D006, C04); the step signs in or skips | — | **changed** (P19): no local account, streaks or reminders in the wizard |\n| `s.help` | help popover open | UI | wizard store | transient | kept |\n| `s.opened` | \"Open Prisma AIRS\" progress | UI | mirrors the `onboarding` transition | transient | kept |\n| `s.theme` | theme prop | Core | `appearance` | — | kept (observed) |\n\n## R2App — shell (`s.*`)\n\n| Prototype key | Meaning | Owner | Where | Lifetime | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `s.tenant`, `s.byTenant` | active tenant; per-tenant state bag | Core | `ShellSnapshot.active`, per-tenant scopes below | persisted | kept; the bag is replaced by scopes |\n| `s.screen` | destination | Core | `navigate` intent, `ShellSnapshot.features` | session | kept; feature ids gain `home`, `inbox` |\n| `s.theme` | theme | Core | `appearance` | persisted | kept |\n| `s.wizard`, `s.added` | first-run wizard open; add-tenant sheet result | Core / UI | `ShellSnapshot.onboarding`; sheet result is a toast | — | kept |\n| `s.overlayDone` | prototype overlay bookkeeping | **Dropped** | canvas-only | — | dropped |\n| `s.palette`, `s.pq` | palette open, query | UI | shell store | transient | kept |\n| `s.tenantOpen`, `s.guard` | switcher open; switch guard | UI | shell store; guard content from the `SwitchBlocked` refusal (`to`, `pending`, `completion`), rendered by the shell for a switch and by the wizard for a setup completion | transient | kept (I1); completion is the same guarded path (P36) |\n| `s.toast`, `s.toastKind`, `s.undo` | toast text, kind, undo target | UI | shell store, timer | ≤ 6 s | kept (I10) |\n| `s.detail`, `s.sheet` | detail sheet; confirm sheet | UI | shell store modal stack | transient | kept (I8) |\n| `s.explain` | explain-mode toggle | UI | shell store | transient | kept |\n| `s.sel`, `s.itab` | Inbox selection, tab | UI | shell store, keyed by tenant id | transient; a switch round trip keeps it (I2) | kept |\n| `s.product`, `s.exp`, `s.ptab`, `s.allOpen`, `s.adminNav`, `s.adminQ`, `s.tree` | Administration product, expanded set, tab per product, expand-all, nav mode, search, tree | UI | admin store | transient | kept |\n| `s.review`, `s.reviewKind`, `s.reviewFrom`, `s.reviewTenant`, `s.reviewApplied` | review open, kind, origin, bound tenant, applied | Core | `Review` scope (tenant-bound, invalidated on context change) | session | kept; the UI holds only \"open\" |\n| `s.typed` | typed confirmation | UI | admin store | until review exit | kept (I3) |\n| `s.secretVisible` | reveal toggle | **Host** | `RevealSecret` sheet; UI holds nothing | 60 s sheet | **changed** (P2): no web reveal state |\n| `s.credOpen`, `s.credVal` | credential dialog open, value | Host | credential entry is the host secret sheet | — | **changed** (P1): no web credential value |\n| `s.packsOpen`, `s.packPick` | starter-pack dialog, picks | UI → Core | library intent | transient | kept |\n| `s.ncOpen`, `s.ncName`, `s.ncPid`, `s.ncInput`, `s.ncDir` | new-case dialog fields | UI → Core | `createCase` (existing library) | transient | kept |\n| `s.casePage`, `s.caseQ`, `s.cfil` | Test Cases paging, search, filter | UI | Test Cases screen state (keyed by context) | transient | kept |\n| `s.req`, `s.reqQ`, `s.fmt`, `s.rtab`, `s.rsub` | API Client request, search, body format, response tab, sub-tab | UI | workbench store | transient | kept |\n| `s.quiz` | Academy quiz state | **Dropped** | hosted Academy owns it (P19) | — | dropped |\n| `s.convoHint` | ended-conversation hint | UI | harness store; cleared by any navigation; its opening question is the core's `opening` (the conversation's, or the opened saved record's), never the title (P51) | transient | kept |\n| (none; DESIGN-V2 §3) | \"Show the calls\" preference and panel | Core | `ShellSnapshot.showCalls` (the operator's choice once made, else on until onboarding completes) and `ShellSnapshot.calls` (the active tenant's calls this app run: request line, credential kind, header names, status, duration; never a value, query or body) (P54) | preference persisted; calls in memory for the app run | added |\n| `ts.activeCase` hand-off | the case opened in the Playground | UI → Core | shell store `playground` (tenant, case, fields) → Runtime Playground prefill; the scan names the case (`scan.case`) and the core records its result (P55, P56) | until the next hand-off | kept |\n\n## R2App — per-tenant (`ts.*`)\n\n| Prototype key | Meaning | Owner | Where | Lifetime | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `ts.reading`, `ts.reads`, `ts.firstRead`, `ts.lastRead`, `ts.warnCleared`, `ts.capsScan` | read in progress, count, first read done, last-read time, warning cleared, scan capability | Core | `ReadStatus` scope, from the tenant's read record (one per opened tenant, kept across a switch round trip, P37) | session, per tenant | kept (I4); `reads` count is not shown and never feeds a timestamp |\n| `ts.ack`, `ts.snoozed` | acknowledgments, snoozes with return | Core | `InboxEntry.hold` (`acknowledge`, or `snooze` with `returnsAt` computed in the core); intents `acknowledgeItem`/`snoozeItem`/`unsnoozeItem`; the last snooze's `SnoozeReceipt` on the Inbox scope is what the toast announces, once (P38) | session, per tenant (as v1's holds) | kept (I11); not persisted across a relaunch, as the retained holds were not |\n| `ts.prompt`, `ts.dir`, `ts.profile`, `ts.model`, `ts.app`, `ts.kind`, `ts.scanned`, `ts.scanDir`, `ts.scanProfile`, `ts.results`, `ts.activeCase`, `ts.activeInput`, `ts.activeDir` | Playground prompt, direction, profile, model, app, classified kind, scanned flag, scan selectors, per-case results, active case | prompt/dir/profile/model/app: UI; scan result + per-case results: Core | workbench store; `ScanRecordView` (existing) and library case results | prompt transient; results persisted per tenant | kept; verdict computed by the existing scan path, never by a UI classifier (the prototype's `classify` is fixture-only) |\n| `ts.extraCases`, `ts.packs` | user-created cases, packs | Core | library | persisted | kept |\n| `ts.hist` | API responses | Core | workbench history | persisted | kept (I5) |\n| `ts.topicRev`, `ts.topicDesc`, `ts.injApplied`, `ts.aesApplied`, `ts.aesRev` | applied review results | Core | read back from the product scopes after apply | — | kept for Runtime topics; `aes*` **dropped** (P18) |\n| `ts.keyRotated`, `ts.keySecretClosed`, `ts.keyDeployed`, `ts.keyDoneAt` | rotation stage | Core | `Tenant.rotations` → `ShellSnapshot.rotations: RotationView{stage, oldKey, newKey, issuedBy, deploymentAcknowledgedAt, oldKeyRemovedAt, removalRejected}`; stage derived (issuanceUnconfirmed, issued, resumed, acknowledged, removalUnconfirmed, complete); intent `acknowledgeDeployment` | per tenant, persisted (timestamps stored once, and the reviewed key name that alone confirms an unconfirmed issuance); the held secret only on its change result, for its context | **changed** (P20, P41): supported Version → Delete sequence; see screens/reviews-administration.md |\n| `ts.follows` | follow-up status per conversation | Core | sessions | persisted | kept |\n| `ts.convo`, `ts.userConvos`, `ts.msgsBy`, `ts.decs`, `ts.ended`, `ts.archived` | current conversation, user conversations, messages, decisions, ended flags, archives | Core | existing harness sessions and decisions | persisted, protected | kept |\n| `ts.draft` | composer draft | UI | shell store per tenant and workspace ID (`harnessDrafts`), with kept messages (`harnessUnsent`: not sent, or not confirmed until their own conversation reports the core took their send ID, `ConversationView.submissions`) | transient | kept |\n\n## Credential entry paths (native)\n\n| Credential | Entry | Storage | Readable by the web layer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Scan API key | webview password field read through a ref, cleared at once, sent once as `EnteredSecret` inside `configureScanCredential` (P25) | vault (`cr-` record), Keychain v2 namespace | state and mode only (`ScanView`), never the value |\n| Management client secret | same path, `configureManagementCredential` (optional section) | vault | client id and state only |\n| Gateway workspace key | same path, `configureInferenceCredential` | vault | state only |\n| Issued API key (rotation) | `RevealSecret` host sheet / host clipboard | held per result for the active context, never persisted; retired by the review's exit (`DiscardChange` on the applied review, also before the change settles), by acknowledging the deployment, or by a context change | never |\n# First-run wizard and add-tenant sheet\n\nSource: `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html` (steps, `ERR`, `touch`, `vsig`,\n`verify`, `opened`, `railCtx`, `mode=\"add\"`), `R2App` `addtenant` overlay.\nChunk: C29. Realises D013 (scan-key-first onboarding).\n\n## Steps (first run)\n\n1. **Welcome** — explains that the app is built entirely on Palo Alto\n   Networks' public APIs and exists to show application builders what those\n   interfaces make possible; three cards: Built on the public APIs / See the\n   calls as you go / Learn by doing. Continue.\n2. **Tenant** — name, environment (select), region (select), TSG id, then\n   three credential sections in this order (D013, deviation P17):\n   **Scan key** (required on first run): \"Add scan key…\" opens the host\n   secret sheet and returns a vault id shown as a masked indicator.\n   **Management client** (optional): client id field plus \"Add client\n   secret…\" (host secret sheet); without it Administration is read-only and\n   says so. **Gateway** (optional toggle): workspace name, endpoint URL,\n   \"Add workspace key…\". Secondary action \"Import from Prisma AIRS Desktop\n   v1\" fills name/environment/TSG from the import intent; secrets are always\n   re-entered. Validation per field on blur with\n   `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`; the Continue button names what is\n   missing. After this step the rail shows \"Name · Environment · TSG …\" under\n   its title.\n3. **Products** — cards for the products in DESIGN-V2 §6. Admitted products\n   show licence state read from the tenant and are selectable; Red Team and\n   Model/skill are marked read-only; Agentic Identity Security and Agentic\n   Endpoint Security are shown as \"Not available in this release\" and cannot\n   be selected (P18).\n4. **Verify** — dispatch `verifyTenantSetup`; per-product rows fill as\n   `VerifyStep` results stream (pass / warning / fail with reason) using the\n   existing reads for each admitted product (scan capability check, a\n   management read when a client is present, Gateway prerequisites).\n   Unavailable products show \"Not available\", never a result. The warning\n   and failed rows are fixtures on admitted products. Fail offers \"Fix and verify\n   again\" (returns to Tenant) or \"Continue with warnings\"; warnings become\n   Inbox items on completion.\n5. **Starter packs** (optional) — test-case packs per selected product with\n   counts.\n6. **Academy account** (optional) — sign in or skip; the trust copy states\n   exactly what syncs (Academy progress only).\n7. **Done** — summary; \"Open Prisma AIRS\" is finite (`opening` → done) and\n   dispatches `completeOnboarding`.\n\n## Add-tenant sheet (`mode=\"add\"`)\n\n- 1160×780 sheet over the shell, rail 244px, no Welcome or Academy steps,\n  Cancel at every step; completion dispatches `addTenant` then `switchTenant`.\n  Cancel discards everything except a credential already written by the\n  secret sheet, which is shown in Administration as unattached and can be\n  removed there.\n\n## Core contract\n\n- `verifyTenantSetup{draft}` → stream of `VerifyStep{product, state, reason}`\n  then `VerifyDone{warnings}`.\n- `completeOnboarding{name, env, region, tsg, scan_credential_id,\n  management: {client_id, credential_id}?, gateway: {ws, endpoint,\n  credential_id}?, products, packs, academy_opt_in, warnings}` writes the tenant profile, product\n  selection, packs and Inbox warning items; sets `onboarding=done`.\n- `addTenant{...same minus academy}`.\n- The core never receives a secret through these intents; `credential_ids`\n  reference vault records created by the host secret sheet.\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Boards: see [boards.md](boards.md) (`fx.on.*`, `fx.addTenant`).\n- Tests: step validation and invalidation signature; streaming verify order;\n  cancel semantics; `onboarding` transitions; V2-N02.\n- Live (C29 only): verify against Vulture, reads only, under the designated\n  scope.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
