{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/planning/test-catalogue.md; cat docs/planning/chunks/C43.md; rg -n '200|clip|T09|C29-N0|C43-N0' docs/architecture/native-acceptance.md docs/architecture/native-checks.json apps/desktop/src/v2/v2.css apps/desktop/src/v2/*.css; sed -n '930,1128p' apps/desktop/src/v2/wizard/wizard.tsx\"","aggregated_output":"# Behavioral and native test catalogue\n\nThese are required future tests and observable assertions, not results already\nexecuted. G01/C01 bind them to exact commands. Each chunk names its applicable\nIDs and adds feature-specific cases. Use fake transports/clocks/stores at real\nmodule interfaces plus literal external fixtures; native and live tests provide\nseparate evidence. Do not assert implementation-private structure for its own sake.\n\n## Core authority and SDK\n\n- **T01 Context isolation:** tenant/workspace/credential switch during a request\n  rejects old replies, retires pending reviews/one-time secrets, and cancels work.\n  Switching back cannot revive authority. Credential replacement and sign-out\n  behave the same way; duplicate completions settle at most once.\n- **T02 Review authority:** forged/stale/replayed/consumed review IDs, changed\n  draft/resource/context, model text, and imported history cannot Apply. Valid\n  operator Apply transmits the exact reviewed operation once.\n- **T03 Unknown outcomes:** disconnect before send, after send, timeout, cancel,\n  401/403/429/5xx, and partial multistep provisioning yield correct states. No\n  automatic mutation/scan replay; offer readback/review/explicit retry where valid.\n- **T04 SDK external contract:** independently authored request/response fixtures\n  verify method/path/body/headers/options, pagination/multipart limits, unknown\n  enum/action preservation, sanitized errors, and no dropped options.\n- **T05 Credential confinement:** scan-only setup works; management/inference/MCP\n  credentials are separate. Deny wrong-origin redirects or custom endpoint\n  changes that would forward a credential without an explicitly reviewed new\n  destination binding. Preserve legitimate operator-reviewed endpoint overrides\n  and explicitly selected nonsecret tenant-profile import; whitelist metadata,\n  discard embedded secrets and never follow credential-file references.\n  No implicit environment/tenant file\n  loading, upstream fallback, persistent renderer storage, or secret log fields.\n- **T06 Protected storage:** locked/denied/unavailable/corrupt store, interrupted\n  write/reset, session-only mode, restart, explicit one-time reveal/clipboard,\n  and cleanup. No plaintext fallback; v1 namespaces remain untouched.\n- **T07 Lifecycle:** bounded concurrent work, cancellation, queue backpressure,\n  superseding reads, app close/restart, sleep/wake, expired credentials, and\n  monotonic versus wall-clock decisions. UI remains responsive during work.\n\n## Presentation and Academy\n\n- **T08 Shared presentation:** web and desktop consumers build from the same\n  reviewed shared source; themes/fonts/routes render correctly. General desktop\n  screens mount no Academy gamification/account effects or web manager routes.\n- **T09 Native UI:** actual Tauri command path, menus/shortcuts, keyboard-only\n  workflow, focus restoration, VoiceOver labels/order, zoom/large text, themes,\n  reduced motion, long/empty/error content, and window resizing. Mock IPC tests\n  alone cannot establish these. macOS WebDriver availability must be verified;\n  use supported native accessibility/automation or recorded manual steps.\n- **T10 Academy identity:** device grant, pending/slow_down/expiry/cancel, refresh,\n  revocation, wrong issuer/client/scope, account switch/sign-out, and stale replies.\n  Token management stays Rust-owned. The learner account is independent of tenant.\n- **T11 Learning authority:** client bundles contain no answer keys/private lab\n  evaluation, privileged routes, or assessor tokens. Forged verdict/award/local\n  exam clock cannot pass; the hosted backend decides access, grading, and awards.\n  Signed-in denial differs from guest sign-in; sandbox never uses tenant secrets.\n- **T12 Offline work:** download lease/revision/account access, encrypted draft\n  save/restart, locked vault, sign-out/account switch, withdrawn content, duplicate\n  submission IDs, changed draft versions, and reconnection. No deferred action\n  replay. Valid local work remains usable without claiming offline grading.\n\n## Workflows and Harness\n\n- **T13 Collection semantics:** exact capability subsets, large collections,\n  bounded pagination/truncation, search/filter/page resets, stale/partial cache,\n  consistent Home/Inbox source facts, and no false complete/zero/absent claims.\n- **T14 API Client documents:** edit/save/conflict while typing, invalid input,\n  environment/secret separation, import/path traversal/size errors, multipart,\n  cookies/redirect auth, cancellation, history/download, Git/profile adoption,\n  and recovery from interrupted writes. Arbitrary workbench targets cannot borrow\n  privileged application credentials through renderer-supplied references.\n- **T15 Harness process:** actual native binary and bounded bootstrap/JSONL\n  protocol, malformed/oversized frames, correlation/duplicates, queue pressure,\n  crash/EOF/cancel, context change, graceful/forced cleanup, and missing/tampered\n  resources. No PATH launcher fallback or plaintext rollout/history.\n- **T16 Harness authority:** typed investigation/proposal tools, active-draft\n  protection, no engine Apply, one-time secrets absent from model context,\n  read-only project defaults, approved single-process command restrictions,\n  forbidden descendants/pipelines, stale decisions, and history replay.\n- **T17 Inference/MCP identity:** pinned Gateway origin; SSO PKCE/state/nonce/\n  issuer/client/audience/time/signature/JWKS/algorithm/key-rotation validation;\n  sleep/refresh/revoke/identity changes;\n  distinct inference/MCP grants; fixed conversation server scope; exact call-item\n  approvals; changed revision/grant; denied tools; trace/execution evidence.\n  No direct upstream provider fallback or global cross-workspace MCP authority.\n\n## Import, quality, and artifacts\n\n- **T18 Import transaction:** dry-run selection, versions/source lock, account\n  match, protected source reads, malformed/oversized/traversal inputs, interruption\n  at each commit point, restart, duplicate import, destination conflict, rollback,\n  and source-byte preservation. No credentials/sessions/approvals transfer.\n- **T19 Diagnostics privacy:** seeded canary secrets and customer content absent\n  from logs/crash files/exports by default; explicit redacted export; correct\n  retention/reset; no analytics/crash upload attempts; encrypted user history\n  remains a distinct intentional storage feature.\n- **T20 Performance:** named macOS hardware/OS/workloads, cold/warm startup, idle\n  and scan/large-list/streaming/Harness memory, main-thread responsiveness, file\n  and DMG footprint. Record methodology, repetitions, distribution and baseline;\n  set core budgets in C03 and register later workload budgets at the introducing\n  chunk's entry before implementation/acceptance measurement. See the budget\n  governance below; C24/C26 compare with pre-registered values.\n- **T21 Controlled live:** designated account/tenant/entitlements and disposable\n  resources, explicit operation allowlist/budgets, sanitized request IDs, readback,\n  cleanup receipts, deny/error cases, and unresolved outcome handling. Missing\n  access or unsupported operations remain blocked; no destructive production tests.\n- **T22 Installed package:** signed/notarized/stapled DMG, Gatekeeper/quarantine,\n  mount/drag/install/launch/relaunch with fresh user/home and no developer checkout,\n  PATH Node/Bun/managed CLI disabled, actual Rust sidecar, runtime inventory/hash\n  integrity, no hidden backend download, safe uninstall/reset/coexistence,\n  manual update, previous-version rollback, and preserved user work.\n- **T23 Cross-feature offline:** launch offline and read/edit each applicable\n  local category: saved cases, FP/FN reports, API Client documents, protected\n  Harness history, configuration drafts, and Academy work. Mark remote data as\n  stale/unknown as appropriate. Offline drafts do not retain valid Apply authority;\n  reconnect requires fresh readback/review when needed. Pending reviews, scans,\n  inference turns, generic HTTP mutations and MCP/tool calls never resubmit on\n  reconnect. Offer explicit retry while preserving uncertain remote outcomes.\n  Bind to C03,C09–C12,C14–C15,C17–C18,C20–C22 and cumulative C24.\n\n## Performance budget governance\n\nC03 registers numeric budgets and named methods for the shell/scan workloads\nbefore C04. Also register the later workload catalogue and owning chunks.\nBefore implementing/measuring a newly introduced workload, its owning chunk\ncommits a numeric budget, hardware/OS, dataset, measurement method and rationale:\nC11/C13 large collections; C15 large HTTP bodies/downloads; C18 streaming/charts;\nC19 native-engine startup/memory; C20 history; C21/C22 tool/MCP workloads.\nDo not wait until C24 to fit limits to observed results.\n\nA budget change requires a versioned rationale, original failures/results, and\nowner or independent reviewer acknowledgement recorded in the receipt. It cannot\nsilently erase a regression. Benchmark evidence records the pre-registered budget\nhash; the controller rejects retroactive or mismatched budget inputs. C24/C26\ncompare against those exact pre-committed values, including changed-budget history.\n\nNormal bounded metadata reads or credential refresh prerequisites for an explicit\noperation are not deferred business-action replay. Tests must distinguish these\nfrom silently resubmitting scans, writes, grading, or tool calls after reconnect.\n\nBefore review, challenge security-critical tests with a relevant deliberate\nbehavior mutation or equivalent negative probe. Show that violating an invariant\nfails the test; do not create an exhaustive mutation framework or mirror every\nimplementation detail. Run mutations only in isolated disposable copies.\n# C43 — Wizard re-port\n\nPhase: P09 (re-cut, D059). Status: planned. Required predecessor: C42.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe screen matches its prototype board side by side at 1440×900 in light and dark with real core data, as the owner approved from the chunk's composites, and passes its gate at 8.\n\n## The board\n\nR2Onboard, every `step`, `filled`, `verify`, `mode=add`. The frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is the specification; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md` states the bar.\n\n## Regions to port\n\nthe presentation re-ported over the existing state machine and intents: 320px rail (244px in add mode) with brand tile, numbered steps, done checks, Optional/Skipped tags, privacy note and theme button; a pinned footer (Cancel in add mode, Back, hint, Step n of m, Skip, primary); section cards (18/20), a 2-column field grid, segmented control, switch; each step's layout per the board; the add sheet at a fixed 1160×780 without the modal's padding. Model-driven extras (credential save/remove forms, workspace chooser, unavailable products) housed inside the prototype's cards.\n\n## Core it reads\n\n`ShellSnapshot.setup`; the setup intents of C29 unchanged. No new core capability unless named here; v2 components import no legacy feature view.\n\n## Parity\n\nComposites at `docs/planning/evidence/C43/parity/<board>-<theme>.png` (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C43-N01 every step first-run; C43-N02 the add sheet; C43-N03 keyboard, ring, 900×600 at 200% both themes), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_wizard` (C29's `ui_v2_onboarding` stays registered); Vitest `v2/wizard/*.test.tsx`.\nzsh:1: no matches found: apps/desktop/src/v2/*.css\n                                <div className='grid' style={{ gridTemplateColumns: 'minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr)', gap: 14 }}>\n                                    {card(\n                                        <>\n                                            <b className='text-[14px]'>{C.academy.account}</b>\n                                            <AcademyAccount view={snapshot.academy} dispatch={dispatch} />\n                                        </>,\n                                        {},\n                                        { 'data-slot': 'academy-card' }\n                                    )}\n                                    {card(\n                                        <>\n                                            <b className='text-[14px]'>{C.academy.whatSyncs}</b>\n                                            <ul className='flex list-disc flex-col pl-5 text-[13px]' style={{ gap: 6, color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                                                {C.academy.syncs.map((t) => (\n                                                    <li key={t}>{t}</li>\n                                                ))}\n                                            </ul>\n                                        </>,\n                                        { gap: 10 },\n                                        { 'data-slot': 'academy-syncs' }\n                                    )}\n                                </div>\n                            </>\n                        )}\n                        {step === 'done' && setup && (\n                            <div className='flex flex-col' style={{ gap: 16, paddingTop: 10 }}>\n                                <span className='grid place-items-center rounded-[18px]' style={{ width: 64, height: 64, background: 'var(--v2-ok-bg)', color: 'var(--v2-ok)' }}>\n                                    <Glyph name='check' size={34} color='var(--v2-ok)' />\n                                </span>\n                                <h1 ref={heading} id={headingId} tabIndex={-1} className='font-bold' style={{ fontSize: 30, letterSpacing: '-0.02em' }}>\n                                    {C.done.title(setup.tenant.label)}\n                                </h1>\n                                <p className='text-[15px]' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                                    {C.done.lead}\n                                </p>\n                                <div className='flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-[12px] border' style={{ borderColor: 'var(--v2-rule)', background: 'var(--v2-paper)' }} data-slot='summary'>\n                                    {(\n                                        [\n                                            [C.done.summary.tenant, railCtx, 'ok', 'tenant'],\n                                            [C.done.summary.scan, scanReady ? C.done.summary.saved : C.done.summary.notSaved, scanReady ? 'ok' : 'skip', 'tenant'],\n                                            [C.done.summary.client, clientReady ? C.done.summary.saved : C.done.summary.notSaved, clientReady ? 'ok' : 'skip', 'tenant'],\n                                            [C.done.summary.products, setup.products.map(productLabel).join(', '), 'ok', 'products'],\n                                            [C.done.summary.checks, ...checksSummary(run), 'verify'],\n                                            [C.done.summary.packs, selectedPacks.length ? selectedPacks.map(productLabel).join(', ') : C.done.summary.none, selectedPacks.length ? 'ok' : 'skip', 'packs'],\n                                            ...(isAdd ? [] : [[C.done.summary.academy, snapshot.academy.state === 'signedIn' ? snapshot.academy.displayName : C.done.summary.academySkipped, snapshot.academy.state === 'signedIn' ? 'ok' : 'skip', 'academy']]),\n                                        ] as [string, string, 'ok' | 'warn' | 'skip', WizardStep][]\n                                    ).map(([k, v, tone, target], i) => (\n                                        <div key={k} className='flex items-center' style={{ gap: 12, padding: '12px 18px', borderTop: i ? '1px solid var(--v2-rule)' : 0 }}>\n                                            <span className='grid shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full' style={{ width: 26, height: 26, background: tone === 'ok' ? 'var(--v2-ok-bg)' : tone === 'warn' ? 'var(--v2-flag-bg)' : 'var(--v2-inset)', color: tone === 'ok' ? 'var(--v2-ok)' : tone === 'warn' ? 'var(--v2-flag)' : 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                                                <Glyph name={tone === 'ok' ? 'check' : tone === 'warn' ? 'alert' : 'dot'} size={13} color={tone === 'ok' ? 'var(--v2-ok)' : tone === 'warn' ? 'var(--v2-flag)' : 'var(--v2-soft)'} />\n                                            </span>\n                                            <span className='font-semibold' style={{ width: 130 }}>\n                                                {k}\n                                            </span>\n                                            <span className='sr-only'>: </span>\n                                            <span className='min-w-0 flex-grow' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                                                {v}\n                                            </span>\n                                            <button type='button' onClick={() => reachable(steps.indexOf(target)) && go(steps.indexOf(target))} className='text-[12px] font-semibold' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-acc)' }} aria-label={`${C.done.change} ${k}`}>\n                                                {C.done.change}\n                                            </button>\n                                        </div>\n                                    ))}\n                                </div>\n                                <div className='grid' style={{ gridTemplateColumns: 'repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr))', gap: 12 }} data-slot='next-up'>\n                                    {C.done.nextUp.map((n) => (\n                                        <div key={n.title} className='flex flex-col rounded-[12px] border' style={{ gap: 8, padding: '18px 20px', borderColor: 'var(--v2-rule)', background: 'var(--v2-paper)' }}>\n                                            <span className='grid place-items-center rounded-[8px]' style={{ width: 28, height: 28, background: 'var(--v2-acc-soft)', color: 'var(--v2-acc)' }}>\n                                                <Glyph name={n.icon} size={14} color='var(--v2-acc)' />\n                                            </span>\n                                            <b>{n.title}</b>\n                                            <span className='leading-[1.45]' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                                                {n.text}\n                                            </span>\n                                        </div>\n                                    ))}\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        )}\n                    </section>\n                </main>\n                <footer className='flex shrink-0 flex-wrap items-center' style={{ gap: 10, padding: isAdd ? '14px 32px' : '14px 44px', borderTop: '1px solid var(--v2-rule)', background: 'var(--v2-bg)' }} data-slot='wizard-footer'>\n                    {isAdd && (\n                        <button type='button' onClick={() => void cancel()} disabled={cancelling} className='h-8 rounded-[7px] border px-3.5 text-[13px] disabled:opacity-60' style={{ borderColor: 'var(--v2-rule)', background: 'var(--v2-paper)' }}>\n                            {cancelling ? C.cancelling : C.cancel}\n                        </button>\n                    )}\n                    {showBack && (\n                        <button type='button' onClick={() => go(index - 1)} className='h-8 rounded-[7px] border px-3.5 text-[13px]' style={{ borderColor: 'var(--v2-rule)', background: 'var(--v2-paper)' }}>\n                            {C.back}\n                        </button>\n                    )}\n                    <p role='status' aria-live='polite' data-slot='wizard-status' className='flex min-w-0 items-center text-[12.5px]' style={{ gap: 10, color: status ? 'var(--v2-ink)' : 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                        <span className='min-w-0'>{status?.text ?? hint}</span>\n                        {status?.retry && <Secondary label={C.outcome.retry} onClick={status.retry} />}\n                    </p>\n                    <span className='ml-auto text-[12px]' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-faint)' }} data-slot='wizard-progress'>\n                        {C.progress(index + 1, steps.length)}\n                    </span>\n                    {extra && <Secondary label={extra.label} onClick={extra.onClick} disabled={extra.disabled} />}\n                    {secondary && <Secondary label={secondary.label} onClick={secondary.onClick} disabled={secondary.disabled} />}\n                    {skipBtn && <Secondary label={skipBtn.label} onClick={skipBtn.onClick} disabled={skipBtn.disabled} />}\n                    <button type='button' onClick={primary.onClick} disabled={primary.disabled} className='h-8 rounded-[7px] px-[18px] text-[13px] font-semibold disabled:opacity-60' style={{ background: 'var(--v2-acc)', color: 'var(--v2-acc-ink)' }} data-slot='wizard-primary'>\n                        {primary.label}\n                    </button>\n                </footer>\n            </div>\n            {/* The guard is a dialog above the sheet (I8): rendered at the body, outside the sheet's inert subtree. */}\n            {completionGuard && setup && createPortal(<SwitchGuard target={setup.tenant.label} completion onStay={() => void dispatch({ kind: 'dismissSwitchGuard' })} onResolve={(resolution) => void finish(resolution)} />, document.body)}\n        </div>\n    )\n}\n\n/** A section card with a switch in its header (R2Onboard's optional cards); a required card has no switch and stays open. */\nfunction OptionalCard({ icon, title, text, tag, open, onToggle, switchLabel, state, slot, onSubmit, busy, children }: { icon: GlyphName; title: string; text: string; tag: string; open: boolean; onToggle?: (on: boolean) => void; switchLabel?: string; state?: ReactNode; slot: string; onSubmit?: (e: FormEvent<HTMLFormElement>) => void; busy?: boolean; children: ReactNode }) {\n    const Tag = onSubmit ? 'form' : 'section'\n    return (\n        <Tag onSubmit={onSubmit} aria-busy={onSubmit ? busy : undefined} aria-label={onSubmit ? undefined : title} className='flex flex-col rounded-[12px] border' style={{ gap: 12, padding: '18px 20px', borderColor: 'var(--v2-rule)', background: 'var(--v2-paper)' }} data-slot={slot}>\n            <div className='flex items-center' style={{ gap: 12 }}>\n                <span className='grid shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-[8px]' style={{ width: 30, height: 30, background: 'var(--v2-inset)', color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                    <Glyph name={icon} size={15} color='var(--v2-soft)' />\n                </span>\n                <span className='min-w-0 flex-grow'>\n                    <span className='flex items-center' style={{ gap: 8 }}>\n                        <b className='text-[14px]'>{title}</b>\n                        <span className='rounded-full text-[12px] font-semibold' style={{ padding: '1px 7px', background: 'var(--v2-inset)', color: 'var(--v2-faint)' }}>\n                            {tag}\n                        </span>\n                        {state}\n                    </span>\n                    <span className='text-[12px]' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n                        {text}\n                    </span>\n                </span>\n                {onToggle && (\n                    <button type='button' role='switch' aria-checked={open} aria-label={switchLabel ?? title} onClick={() => onToggle(!open)} className='relative shrink-0 rounded-full' style={{ width: 38, height: 22, border: 0, background: open ? 'var(--v2-acc)' : 'var(--v2-inset)', boxShadow: `inset 0 0 0 1px ${open ? 'var(--v2-acc)' : 'var(--v2-ctl)'}` }} data-slot='switch'>\n                        <span className='absolute rounded-full' style={{ top: 3, left: open ? 19 : 3, width: 16, height: 16, background: open ? 'var(--v2-acc-ink)' : 'var(--v2-paper)' }} />\n                    </button>\n                )}\n            </div>\n            {open && (\n                <div className='flex flex-col' style={{ gap: 10, paddingLeft: 42 }}>\n                    {children}\n                </div>\n            )}\n        </Tag>\n    )\n}\n\nfunction Field({ label, name, hint, error, onBlur, value, onChange, ...rest }: { label: string; name: string; hint?: string; error?: string; onBlur?: (value: string) => void; value?: string; onChange?: (value: string) => void; maxLength?: number; inputMode?: 'numeric' }) {\n    const id = useId()\n    return (\n        <label className='flex flex-col text-[12px] font-semibold' style={{ gap: 5, color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n            {label}\n            <input id={id} name={name} autoComplete='off' value={value} onChange={onChange ? (e) => onChange(e.target.value) : undefined} aria-invalid={error ? true : undefined} aria-describedby={error ? `${id}-error` : hint ? `${id}-hint` : undefined} onBlur={(e) => onBlur?.(e.target.value)} className='h-8 min-h-0 rounded-[7px] border px-2.5 text-[13px] font-normal' style={{ borderColor: error ? 'var(--v2-block)' : 'var(--v2-ctl)', background: 'var(--v2-bg)', color: 'var(--v2-ink)' }} {...rest} />\n            {error ? (\n                <span id={`${id}-error`} role='alert' className='font-normal' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-block)' }}>\n                    {error}\n                </span>\n            ) : hint ? (\n                <span id={`${id}-hint`} className='font-normal' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-faint)' }}>\n                    {hint}\n                </span>\n            ) : null}\n        </label>\n    )\n}\n\n/** A password field read once through its ref and cleared by the caller (P25). */\nfunction SecretField({ label, inputRef, error }: { label: string; inputRef: React.RefObject<HTMLInputElement | null>; error?: string }) {\n    const id = useId()\n    return (\n        <label className='flex flex-col text-[12px] font-semibold' style={{ gap: 5, color: 'var(--v2-soft)' }}>\n            {label}\n            <input id={id} ref={inputRef} type='password' autoComplete='off' aria-invalid={error ? true : undefined} aria-describedby={error ? `${id}-error` : undefined} className='h-8 min-h-0 rounded-[7px] border px-2.5 text-[13px] font-normal' style={{ borderColor: error ? 'var(--v2-block)' : 'var(--v2-ctl)', background: 'var(--v2-bg)', color: 'var(--v2-ink)' }} />\n            {error && (\n                <span id={`${id}-error`} role='alert' className='font-normal' style={{ color: 'var(--v2-block)' }}>\n                    {error}\n                </span>\n            )}\n        </label>\n    )\n}\n\nfunction Primary({ label, disabled }: { label: string; disabled?: boolean }) {\n    return (\n        <button type='submit' disabled={disabled} className='h-8 rounded-[7px] px-4 text-[13px] font-semibold disabled:opacity-60' style={{ background: 'var(--v2-acc)', color: 'var(--v2-acc-ink)' }}>\n            {label}\n        </button>\n    )\n}\n\nfunction Secondary({ label, onClick, disabled }: { label: string; onClick: () => void; disabled?: boolean }) {\n    return (\n        <button type='button' onClick={onClick} disabled={disabled} className='h-8 rounded-[7px] border px-3 text-[13px] disabled:opacity-60' style={{ borderColor: 'var(--v2-rule)', background: 'var(--v2-paper)', color: 'var(--v2-ink)' }}>\n            {label}\n        </button>\n    )\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
