ept after the transcript drops its oldest entries. An archived conversation's record is read for it when the restart is asked for (nothing is filled in meanwhile); choosing another investigation, sending, opening a transcript, a new arrival or another workspace retires that read (a late result changes nothing); otherwise it settles by the core's receipt for the record (`HarnessHistoryView.lastOpen`: id, admission order, failure), newer than any open settled before it was asked for, never by a busy edge or a changed error. When it is not known (a record saved before C32 whose transcript no longer holds its first message) or the record cannot be read, the page says so and never fills in the title instead; a draft in the box is kept under Not sent and nothing is sent | The title is shortened (72 or 80 characters, one line) and lost the rest of a long or multi-line question; the attempt-12 review found the restart prefilling it |\n| P52 | The API Client re-skinned to the prototype's layout (request tree, tabs, method/URL line, 40% response pane) | The v2 API Client presents the C14/C15 workbench in the v2 layout through a layout context its wrapper provides (`shell/presentation.ts` `V2Layout`): the page heading becomes the v2 title row (no kicker), and the request editor puts the method, URL, Send and Save on one compact line with the request details beside a response pane (stacked when narrow). Collections, tabs, history, reviews and execution are the existing components and authority, unchanged; the legacy shell keeps its layout. Send's completion is announced in the editor's status region as \"<request> · <code> · <duration>\", the body outside it, in the response pane (known gap 5, V2-T14). The collection tree and tab strip keep the workbench's own arrangement | The workbench view itself is held by uncommitted owner work in this tree and is not edited; its layout is changed only through the components it renders |\n| P53 | \"Generic requests … refused by the core as