{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\| P(1[789]|2[5-9]|3[012]) ' docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md; sed -n '330,616p' crates/desktop-core/tests/ui_v2_onboarding/main.rs\"","aggregated_output":"30:| P17 | Wizard tenant step requires a management OAuth client id and secret (`ERR.clientId`, `ERR.secret`) and makes the scan key optional (`scanOn`) | First run requires the scan key and makes the management client an optional second section; add mode keeps both optional. Secrets enter only through the host secret sheet | D013 (scan-key-first; management credentials are separate and never imply scan authentication) |\n31:| P18 | Six products are verified, inventoried and administered (AIS tool policies, AES discovered AI and policies, AES policy review `REVIEWS.aes`) | Only products with an admitted service are verified, inventoried or changed: Runtime Security (`ManagementResource`, `ChangeKind`), Gateway (`GatewayRead`, Gateway `ChangeKind`s), Red Team and Model/skill reads (C13, read-only). Agentic Identity Security and Agentic Endpoint Security render as \"Not available in this release\" with their dependency gate; no inventory, verification result or mutation is invented for them | The existing interfaces do not supply those product APIs; fixtures cannot establish a capability (parity matrix, C13 rule) |\n32:| P19 | Wizard Academy step creates a local account with streaks, reminders and a quiz (`s.acad`, `s.af`, `s.streaks`, `s.remind`, `s.quiz`) | The step signs in to the hosted Academy identity or skips; the embedded learner view owns progress and gamification | D004–D006, C04 |\n38:| P25 | Revision of P1/P2: \"secrets enter only through a host secret sheet\" | The retained, reviewed entry path (C02/C09) is a webview password field read through a ref, cleared immediately and sent once inside the intent as `EnteredSecret` (zeroized, never in React state, never logged); the host owns the *reveal* sheet (`RevealSecret`) and the clipboard. C29 uses exactly this path for the scan key, management secret and Gateway key; no new host entry sheet is built | The C27 spec assumed an entry sheet the host does not have; the reviewed pattern already satisfies D014 and the C24 canary checks (no secret in any AX tree or file) |\n39:| P26 | `verifyTenantSetup` as one core intent streaming `VerifyStep`s (wizard.md) | Implemented as specified: `verifyTenantSetup{context}` runs in the core over the draft, admits the reads it needs through the management pipeline (management verify; the chosen Gateway workspace's prerequisites, or only the listing when none is chosen, reported as incomplete coverage; Red Team; model/skill) and settles each line from the result; AIS/AES are listed as not available and never read; the lines, `done`, `failed`, `blocking` and `stale` stream through `ShellSnapshot.setup.verify`. The scan key has no admitted read: its line is `stored`, never `pass`. Only the scan key (first run) blocks; an optional service's failure is carried as a warning the operator may continue over | Attempt-01 composed the reads in the presentation; attempt-02 read only the workspace listing and blocked on every failure — both rejected |\n40:| P27 | Add-tenant Cancel writes nothing except an already-vaulted credential | The wizard works on a core-owned draft (`beginTenantSetup`) with its own context and its own Gateway listing and choice; credentials attach to the draft; nothing is listed as a tenant (a draft id is refused by `selectTenant`/`deleteTenant`), the active tenant and its Gateway choice are untouched until `completeTenantSetup` commits the draft in one step and switches once. Every change to the draft's credentials or profile retires its context (and the binding, reads and listing under it). Cancel (`discardTenantSetup`) drops the draft, retires the binding and every read under its context and workspace reference, and queues its Keychain records for cleanup; the sheet closes only once the core admits it (a creation still pending or unconfirmed is awaited and whatever it produced is discarded). A relaunch, or a tenant committed outside the wizard during first run, does the same | Stronger than the spec's leftover credential: no orphan secrets and no cached authority surviving a replaced credential |\n41:| P28 | Gateway workspace key entered on the wizard tenant step | Implemented: an optional section reads the workspaces through the management client (`management` gateway inventory on the draft context), `selectGatewayWorkspace` chooses one, and `configureInferenceCredential` saves the endpoint and key for it | The admitted sequence (list → select → key) runs on the draft like on a tenant |\n42:| P29 | \"Import from v1\" fills the tenant step in place | The action navigates to the reviewed import destination (C23), which renders on its own during first run with a 'Back to setup' control; the wizard resumes afterwards | The import review flow is itself reviewed and must not be duplicated inside the wizard |\n43:| P30 | The wizard opens whenever onboarding is not done | The shell shows onboarding as done whenever a tenant already exists (an upgrade, or a tenant created before the v2 shell was chosen); the stored state is untouched. A first run is one with no tenant yet; a relaunch mid-setup reopens at the Tenant step with a fresh draft (the previous draft's credentials are cleaned up) | Existing users must never be sent through the wizard; a half-made draft is never a tenant |\n44:| P31 | Products step shows licence state read from the tenant | No admitted service reports licensing (DESIGN-V2 §6); each card shows what it reads with (scan key / management client, saved or not) and, once verified, that product's verify result; a note says licence state is not readable through the public APIs | Nothing may be inferred about licensing from reads that do not report it |\n45:| P32 | First-run import returns to the wizard | A v1 import during first run commits its tenants through the reviewed C23 flow; the desktop then has a tenant, so the first-run draft ends (its credentials are cleaned up) and the shell opens on the imported tenant; its scan key is added in Administration (the reviewed C08/C09 credential setup) | A tenant that exists is never sent back through a first-run wizard (P30), and the wizard cannot wrap an existing tenant without duplicating it |\n        tenant.scan.state,\n        desktop_core::ScanState::Ready,\n        \"the key moved with it\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        tenant.setup_warnings.len(),\n        2,\n        \"management + gateway warnings\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(tenant.setup_warnings[0].id, \"vw-1\");\n    assert_eq!(tenant.setup_warnings[1].product, ProductId::Gateway);\n    assert!(tenant.setup_warnings[0].recorded_secs > 1_700_000_000);\n    assert_eq!(\n        snap.active.as_ref().map(|a| &a.tenant),\n        Some(&tenant.id),\n        \"active once\"\n    );\n    assert_ne!(\n        snap.active.as_ref().map(|a| a.context.as_str()),\n        Some(context.as_str()),\n        \"a fresh context, not the draft's\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(snap.onboarding, OnboardingState::Done);\n    assert_eq!(snap.active_feature, desktop_core::features::FeatureId::Home);\n    // The draft's context is retired with it.\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"verifyTenantSetup\", \"context\": context}))\n            .await,\n        Err(Refusal::StaleContext)\n    );\n    let saved = desk.adapters.store.saved().expect(\"saved\");\n    assert!(saved.tenant_draft.is_none());\n    assert_eq!(saved.tenant_warnings.len(), 1);\n    let desk = desk.restart();\n    let snap = desk.snap();\n    assert_eq!(snap.onboarding, OnboardingState::Done);\n    assert_eq!(snap.tenants[0].setup_warnings.len(), 2, \"restored\");\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn add_mode_keeps_the_shell_untouched_until_completion_and_discard_cleans_up() {\n    let mut desk = Desk::new();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"createTenant\", \"profile\": {\n        \"label\": \"First\", \"tsgId\": \"1111111111\", \"destination\": {\"kind\": \"region\", \"region\": \"europe\"}}}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"first tenant\");\n    let before = desk.snap();\n    let first = before.active.clone().expect(\"active\");\n    assert_eq!(\n        before.onboarding,\n        OnboardingState::Done,\n        \"an existing tenant means no wizard\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.send(\n            json!({\"kind\": \"beginTenantSetup\", \"mode\": \"firstRun\", \"profile\": {\n            \"label\": \"X\", \"tsgId\": null, \"destination\": {\"kind\": \"region\", \"region\": \"europe\"}}})\n        )\n        .await,\n        Err(Refusal::InvalidInput),\n        \"first run is impossible once a tenant exists\"\n    );\n    let context = desk.begin(\"add\", \"Second\").await;\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"configureScanCredential\", \"context\": context, \"mode\": \"keychain\", \"key\": KEY}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"key in the Keychain\");\n    desk.settled(true).await;\n    let context = desk.context();\n    let records = desk.adapters.vault.records();\n    assert_eq!(records.len(), 1, \"one Keychain record for the draft\");\n    let during = desk.snap();\n    assert_eq!(during.tenants.len(), 1, \"the shell still lists one tenant\");\n    assert_eq!(\n        during.active,\n        Some(first.clone()),\n        \"the active tenant and context are untouched\"\n    );\n    assert!(\n        !during.setup.as_ref().expect(\"setup\").scan_required,\n        \"add mode: the key is optional\"\n    );\n    // Discard: nothing changed, and the draft's record is queued for cleanup.\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"discardTenantSetup\", \"context\": context}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"discarded\");\n    let after = desk.snap();\n    assert!(after.setup.is_none());\n    assert_eq!(after.tenants.len(), 1);\n    assert_eq!(after.active, Some(first));\n    let saved = desk.adapters.store.saved().expect(\"saved\");\n    assert!(saved.tenant_draft.is_none());\n    assert!(\n        saved\n            .credentials\n            .iter()\n            .all(|c| c.tenant == before.tenants[0].id)\n    );\n    assert!(\n        saved.pending_cleanup.contains(&records[0])\n            || !desk.adapters.vault.records().contains(&records[0]),\n        \"the draft's Keychain record is being removed\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"verifyTenantSetup\", \"context\": context}))\n            .await,\n        Err(Refusal::StaleContext)\n    );\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn add_mode_without_a_key_verifies_with_a_warning_and_completes_switching_once() {\n    let mut desk = Desk::new();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"createTenant\", \"profile\": {\n        \"label\": \"First\", \"tsgId\": \"1111111111\", \"destination\": {\"kind\": \"region\", \"region\": \"europe\"}}}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"first tenant\");\n    let context = desk.begin(\"add\", \"Second\").await;\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"verifyTenantSetup\", \"context\": context}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"verify\");\n    let v = desk.verified().await;\n    assert_eq!(\n        v.steps[0].state,\n        VerifyState::Warning,\n        \"no key is a warning in add mode\"\n    );\n    assert!(desk.setup().completable);\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"completeTenantSetup\", \"context\": context, \"packs\": []}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"completed\");\n    let snap = desk.snap();\n    assert_eq!(snap.tenants.len(), 2);\n    let second = snap\n        .tenants\n        .iter()\n        .find(|t| t.label == \"Second\")\n        .expect(\"second\");\n    assert_eq!(snap.active.as_ref().map(|a| &a.tenant), Some(&second.id));\n    assert_eq!(second.setup_warnings.len(), 1);\n    assert_eq!(snap.onboarding, OnboardingState::Done);\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn a_relaunch_drops_the_draft_and_queues_its_credentials_for_cleanup() {\n    let mut desk = Desk::new();\n    let context = desk.begin(\"firstRun\", \"Northwind Health\").await;\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"configureScanCredential\", \"context\": context, \"mode\": \"keychain\", \"key\": KEY}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"key\");\n    desk.settled(true).await;\n    let saved = desk.adapters.store.saved().expect(\"saved\");\n    assert!(\n        saved.tenant_draft.is_some(),\n        \"the draft is written so its records are known\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(saved.credentials.len(), 1);\n    assert!(saved.tenants.is_empty());\n    let record = saved.credentials[0].record.clone();\n    let mut desk = desk.restart();\n    let snap = desk.snap();\n    assert!(snap.setup.is_none() && snap.tenants.is_empty());\n    assert_eq!(snap.onboarding, OnboardingState::Needed);\n    // The next write carries no draft; its record was queued for cleanup\n    // (and removed by the start-up cleanup, which the fresh vault records).\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"setShowCalls\", \"on\": false}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"saved again\");\n    let saved = desk.adapters.store.saved().expect(\"saved\");\n    assert!(saved.tenant_draft.is_none());\n    assert!(saved.credentials.is_empty());\n    let deleted = desk\n        .adapters\n        .vault\n        .calls()\n        .into_iter()\n        .any(|c| matches!(c, fixtures::VaultCall::Delete(r) if r == record));\n    assert!(\n        deleted || saved.pending_cleanup.contains(&record),\n        \"cleanup reached the vault\"\n    );\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn a_desktop_with_a_tenant_is_never_sent_through_the_wizard() {\n    let mut desk = Desk::new();\n    assert_eq!(desk.snap().onboarding, OnboardingState::Needed);\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"createTenant\", \"profile\": {\n        \"label\": \"Northwind Health\", \"tsgId\": \"1234567890\",\n        \"destination\": {\"kind\": \"region\", \"region\": \"europe\"}}}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"created\");\n    assert_eq!(desk.snap().onboarding, OnboardingState::Done);\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.adapters.store.saved().expect(\"saved\").onboarding,\n        OnboardingState::Needed,\n        \"the stored state is untouched\"\n    );\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"setUiVariant\", \"variant\": \"v2\"}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"v2\");\n    assert_eq!(desk.snap().onboarding, OnboardingState::Done);\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn a_draft_id_is_never_selectable_or_deletable_as_a_tenant() {\n    let mut desk = Desk::new();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"createTenant\", \"profile\": {\n        \"label\": \"First\", \"tsgId\": \"1111111111\", \"destination\": {\"kind\": \"region\", \"region\": \"europe\"}}}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"first tenant\");\n    let before = desk.snap();\n    desk.begin(\"add\", \"Second\").await;\n    let draft_id = desk.setup().tenant.id.as_str().to_owned();\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"selectTenant\", \"tenant\": draft_id}))\n            .await,\n        Err(Refusal::InvalidInput),\n        \"a draft is not a tenant\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"deleteTenant\", \"tenant\": draft_id}))\n            .await,\n        Err(Refusal::InvalidInput)\n    );\n    let after = desk.snap();\n    assert_eq!(after.active, before.active);\n    assert_eq!(after.tenants, before.tenants);\n    let saved = desk.adapters.store.saved().expect(\"saved\");\n    assert_eq!(saved.active_tenant, before.active.map(|a| a.tenant));\n    assert!(\n        saved.tenant_draft.is_some(),\n        \"the draft itself is still there\"\n    );\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn a_tenant_created_outside_the_wizard_ends_a_first_run_draft_and_the_shell_takes_over() {\n    // The v1 import during first run commits tenants through the same path.\n    let mut desk = Desk::new();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"setUiVariant\", \"variant\": \"v2\"}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"v2\");\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"setOnboarding\", \"state\": \"inProgress\"}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"in progress\");\n    let context = desk.begin(\"firstRun\", \"Drafted\").await;\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"configureScanCredential\", \"context\": context, \"mode\": \"keychain\", \"key\": KEY}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"key\");\n    desk.settled(true).await;\n    let record = desk.adapters.vault.records()[0].clone();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"createTenant\", \"profile\": {\n        \"label\": \"Imported\", \"tsgId\": \"2222222222\", \"destination\": {\"kind\": \"region\", \"region\": \"europe\"}}}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"imported tenant\");\n    let snap = desk.snap();\n    assert!(snap.setup.is_none(), \"the first-run draft is over\");\n    assert_eq!(\n        snap.onboarding,\n        OnboardingState::Done,\n        \"a tenant exists: the shell takes over\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(snap.tenants.len(), 1);\n    assert_eq!(snap.tenants[0].label, \"Imported\");\n    let saved = desk.adapters.store.saved().expect(\"saved\");\n    assert!(saved.tenant_draft.is_none());\n    assert!(\n        saved.credentials.is_empty(),\n        \"the draft's record left the ledger\"\n    );\n    let deleted = desk\n        .adapters\n        .vault\n        .calls()\n        .into_iter()\n        .any(|c| matches!(c, fixtures::VaultCall::Delete(r) if r == record));\n    assert!(\n        deleted || saved.pending_cleanup.contains(&record),\n        \"its Keychain record is cleaned up\"\n    );\n    let desk = desk.restart();\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.snap().onboarding,\n        OnboardingState::Done,\n        \"and stays so after a relaunch\"\n    );\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
