{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1166,1194p' docs/architecture/native-checks.json; sed -n '1364,1381p' docs/architecture/native-checks.json; cat docs/architecture/native-acceptance.md; cat docs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-03/README.md; rg --files docs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04\"","aggregated_output":"    \"C29\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C29-N01\",\n        \"check\": \"First run in the v2 presentation (onboarding needed, no tenant) opens on Welcome with the API-builder framing and three cards, no shell rail and no Back; it opens again after a relaunch; 'Set up a tenant' moves to the Tenant step, the heading takes focus, the rail marks the step current, and Continue is disabled naming what is missing ('Create the tenant to continue').\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C29-N02\",\n        \"check\": \"Tenant step: Create tenant with an empty name and a 9-digit TSG marks each field aria-invalid with its message and drafts nothing; a valid name and TSG draft the tenant in the core (status, rail 'Name \\u00b7 Environment \\u00b7 TSG \\u2026', the profile stays editable with 'Save changes', Continue reads 'Save the scan key to continue'); the scan key is typed once into a secure field and attaches to the draft (Saved, Replace/Remove offered, Continue enabled); the management client saves; the Gateway section reads the workspaces through the client, chooses one and saves its key; editing the name updates the rail and keeps the credentials; no secret appears in any AX tree or in a data file outside the Keychain.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C29-N03\",\n        \"check\": \"Products step: Runtime Security is checked and not uncheckable ('Always on'), AIS and AES are 'Not available in this release' with disabled checkboxes, the licence note is shown; Verify shows planned rows ('Not run yet'; AIS/AES 'Not available') with Continue disabled; with the management client replaced by a rejected secret the core-owned run fails that optional line (scan key reported Stored, never Pass) and offers both 'Continue with warnings' and 'Fix and verify again', which returns to the editable Tenant step where the client is replaced; the rerun authenticates with the new secret (management Pass) and reads the chosen workspace's prerequisites (Pass); changing the products afterwards marks the run stale (Continue closed, Done unreachable) until a rerun finishes clean.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C29-N04\",\n        \"check\": \"Starter cases lists one pack per chosen product with its case count, checked; the Academy step is the reviewed account component (sign-in offered, 'syncs your Academy progress only'); Done summarises the draft; 'Open Prisma AIRS' sends one completion intent, after which Home shows the new tenant in the switcher and Test Cases lists the imported cases; a relaunch shows Home, not the wizard.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C29-N05\",\n        \"check\": \"Add a tenant\\u2026 from the switcher opens the sheet as the one topmost modal (244px rail, no Welcome, Academy or Back), keyboard traversal stays inside it; Cancel before a draft changes nothing; a drafted and keyed tenant cancelled leaves the tenant list and the active tenant unchanged and its key gone; a draft without a key (optional in add mode) verifies with a warning, and Finish commits it once, makes it active with a toast and lists it beside the first.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C29-N06\",\n        \"check\": \"T09 matrix: every wizard step and the add sheet captured in light and dark at 100% and 200% zoom; Tab reaches each step's controls; at the 900\\u00d7600 minimum the sheet's Cancel is inside the window once focused (the dialog scrolls within the viewport).\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"C30\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C30-N01\",\n    \"C43\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C43-N01\",\n        \"check\": \"The first-run wizard as the prototype board draws it (R2Onboard, every step): the 320px rail with the brand tile, the numbered steps turning to checks as they are done, the Optional tags on Starter cases and Academy (Skipped once skipped), the privacy note and the appearance button; the pinned footer with Back, the hint, Step n of m, Skip for now and the primary; Welcome (tile, two paragraphs, three cards, no import box (D060)); Connect your tenant (the Tenant card's 2-column grid with the Environment segmented control and the Region select, Create tenant; then the scan key card tagged Required, the Management credentials card with Where do I find these?, the AI Gateway workspace card with its switch); Which products will you manage? (the 3-column product cards as checkboxes, Runtime always on, AIS and AES unavailable, the no-scan-key banner before a key is saved); Check the connection (the status banner, the Checks card with one row per line, Run the checks, Fix and verify again after a failure, Continue with warnings); Load starter test cases (the pack rows as checkboxes with counts, the summary, Skip for now); Join the AI Security Academy (Your account and What is sent cards, Skip for now); <name> is ready (the summary card with Change links, the three next-up cards, Open Prisma AIRS completing once) \\u2014 the C29 behaviour unchanged (D059 parity: the composites under evidence/C43/parity are captured by this script per step, parity/bundle.json rewritten per capture, the owner's judgement recorded in parity/notes.md).\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C43-N02\",\n        \"check\": \"The add-tenant sheet: a 1160\\u00d7780 dialog without the modal's padding, the 244px rail (Tenant, Products, Verify, Starter cases, Done; no Welcome or Academy), Cancel in the footer on every step and no Back on the first; Cancel before a draft sends nothing; a drafted tenant's scan card is Optional and Continue is open; Cancel after a draft discards it in the core; Finish commits once and the sheet closes with the toast.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C43-N03\",\n        \"check\": \"Keyboard and layout (T09): Tab from the rail reaches the step's first field and the footer's primary in order; the focus ring on the primary; the wizard at 1440\\u00d7900 and at 900\\u00d7600 with 200% zoom, in light and dark, on the Tenant and Verify steps, no horizontal page overflow, the footer's primary inside the window and at least 32 CSS px; every row records the WebView's measured size and the viewport from its own tree and asserts them.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"C44\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C44-N01\",\n        \"check\": \"One presentation (P09 closure): the fixture app's first run is the wizard with no Features rail and no 'Use the new interface' switch anywhere; after the tenant is set up, every destination the catalogue lists is opened from the Go menu (Home, Inbox, Harness, Academy, Test Cases, API Client, Administration; Runtime Security, AI Gateway and Red Team & Models opening Administration on their product; Sessions & Reports and Settings framed by the v2 shell (Import from v1 removed, D060)) under the v2 Destinations rail, each captured in light and dark at 1440\\u00d7900 as the whole-app screenshot set under evidence/C44/parity/app, with no plaintext secret and no learner chrome (outside Academy) in any destination's tree; \\u23182 opens the Inbox and \\u2318, Settings through the native menu; the built stylesheet carries the reduced-motion clamp; the bundle is Node-free and no Node, Bun or Deno process runs beside the app; after a quit and relaunch 15 s of startup open no internet socket from the app or its WebKit processes, Home shows with the tenant active and Administration reads with the kept client; every pre-P09 native assertion has its standing in evidence/C44/legacy-script-map.md (exercised by a named v2 check, self-run through legacy_v2 \\u2014 C03, C04, C05, C06, C07, C10, C11, C24 \\u2014 ported into this check, or retired with its reason) and the mapped drivers' records on this bundle bind the gate: an exercised, self-run or ported assertion without a passing target fails this check.\"\n# Native acceptance procedure (T09 and chunk native assertions)\n\n`xtask native --chunk Cxx` builds the fixture-identity app with\n`native-prepare` and records its executable SHA-256. Acceptance is a separate\nrecord, `docs/planning/evidence/Cxx/native-acceptance.json`\n(schema `airs-v2/native-acceptance/1`, parsed strictly by xtask), produced by\nactually driving that exact executable:\n\n- `method: \"cua\"` — automation through macOS accessibility/automation APIs\n  against the real native window (for example REA native UI capture or System\n  Events), with the captured accessibility trees/screenshots stored under\n  `evidence/Cxx/native/`; or\n- `method: \"operator\"` — a person performs the checklist on the real app and\n  records observations per check.\n\nEvery check must report `pass` with an observation and evidence paths. A\n`fail` or `blocked` check, a record naming different executable bytes, or a\nrecord for the production identity fails the gate. Build success, mocked IPC\ntests or reviewer scores never substitute for this record.\n\nPrerequisites on the acceptance host: macOS grants the automation client\n**Accessibility** (to read the AX tree and send key events) and, for\nscreenshots, **Screen Recording**. Without these grants automated acceptance is\nblocked; the operator method remains available.\n\n## Required checks\n\nThe authoritative per-chunk check list is\n[native-checks.json](native-checks.json) (`airs-v2/native-checks/1`). xtask\nrequires the record to contain exactly those IDs, once each, with result\n`pass`, a nonempty observation and at least one evidence file that the review\npacket hash-binds; the record must name the fixture identity and the prepared\nexecutable, whose current bytes are re-hashed at completion. Changing the list\nis a reviewed source change (it is part of the build-flags fingerprint).\n\nC01 covers launch/identity, native menus, keyboard-only navigation and focus,\nthe palette (including native navigation while it is open), unavailable\ndestinations, Rust-owned appearance, the accessibility tree, minimum window\nsize, zoom to 150%/200%, Reduce Motion, absence of Academy gamification, and\nstartup network behavior.\n\nVoiceOver: C01-N08 inspects the accessibility attributes VoiceOver consumes\n(AXRole, AXTitle/AXDescription, AXValue/selected state and element order) and\nrecords exactly which were read. Spoken VoiceOver output is not claimed by an\nattribute inspection; it is recorded only when an operator actually runs\nVoiceOver, and otherwise remains a C24 cumulative item.\n# Worf check attempt-03 — retained failure and fixture correction\n\nThe fresh run passed 17/18 checks on unchanged inputs. `core-fixtures` failed\nall three retained runs in `imports_rollback`; all other checks passed. Original\nlogs, hashes and pre-correction sources remain immutable. The first targeted\ncorrection passed 22/23 and still failed the exhaustive interruption test; the\nsecond targeted run passed all 23, with every test and assertion retained.\n\nThe harness had omitted the production `Core::shutdown()` exit hook, polled\ntemporary receipt JSON before its durable copies/document binding completed,\nand guessed that 400 ms reached every configured interruption point. It now\nuses the real exit hook and confirmed-durable document, and waits for the armed\nfixture cut to fire. A read-only observer is appended under `test-fixtures`\nonly; no production definition, IPC authority or live operation is changed.\n\nThe complete first 19-driver native generation, including its exact executable,\nis preserved under `native-history/Worf-generation-01-complete-20261101`.\nGeneration 02 is rebuilt and must rerun every mapped driver on its new bytes,\nthen fresh checks and actual independent reviews. No old pass is transferred.\nThe fresh before/after build seal is `preparations/worf-02`; its exact source\ndiff and build log are retained. Current audits allow no source exemptions.\n\nNo real credential, alpha data or product endpoint was used. L19's three reads\nremain charged with zero allowance. This correction does not complete P09.\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/diagnosis.json\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/authority-original.rs\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/rustfmt-corrected.log\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/clippy-failed.log\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/correction.json\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/clippy-corrected.log\ndocs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/relocation-proof.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
