{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/planning/evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md docs/planning/evidence/C29/live/L19/additional-grant-01.json docs/planning/evidence/C29/live/L19/additional-grant-01-validation.json; rg -n 'L19|wizard' docs/planning/live-checks.md; rg -n 'L19|wizard|case' crates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs tools/native-acceptance/test_live_c29_l19.py\"","aggregated_output":"# C29 live row: what the owner must designate\n\nC29's required acceptance includes one live read: \"verify against the\ndesignated read-only tenant (Vulture) under the owner scope, recorded as a\nredacted receipt; no writes\" (`chunks/C29.md`). The approved execution\nmanifest (`~/airs-v2-live.json`, `airs-v2/live-manifest/1`, approved\n2026-10-25) designates Vulture (TSG 1852583913, environment test-b) for the\nL18 scan family only. No family permits a management read on Vulture, so the\nwizard's verify read (`management · verify`, the same read L02 runs on\nRedtail) has no designated scope there.\n\nA Keychain item `mgmt-vulture-client-secret` exists under the live service,\nbut a stored secret is not a designation. Per the release contract a family\nwithout designated access is recorded **blocked**, never passed and never\nrun on an undesignated credential.\n\n## What unblocks it\n\nAdd one family to the private manifest and re-run `cargo run -p xtask --\nlive-scope --scope <path>`:\n\n```json\n\"L19\": {\n  \"status\": \"designated\",\n  \"reason\": \"\",\n  \"environment\": \"test-b\",\n  \"credentials\": {\n    \"client_secret\": { \"kind\": \"keychain\", \"service\": \"io.cdot.prisma-airs-desktop.v2.live\", \"account\": \"mgmt-vulture-client-secret\" }\n  },\n  \"nonsecret\": { \"client_id\": \"<Vulture management client id>\", \"tsg_id\": \"1852583913\", \"region\": \"us\" },\n  \"permitted_operations\": [\"one management verify read through the first-run wizard (C29); no inventories, no writes\"],\n  \"disposable_prefix\": null,\n  \"budget\": { \"reads\": 2 },\n  \"cleanup\": [],\n  \"irreversible_exclusions\": [\"no changes of any kind on Vulture\"]\n}\n```\n\nThe run then goes through the real wizard on the fixture build with the\nKeychain reference, and the receipt lands in `live/L19-verify.json` with the\nclient id and TSG only (no token, no secret). Until then `live/blocked.json`\nis the row's record.\n\n## Preparation update — 2026-11-01\n\nThe owner approved adding read-only L19 with the existing Keychain reference,\na maximum of two reads and no inventory browsing or changes. The public client\nID was supplied through the owner's local CLI tenant configuration; its secret\nfield was neither copied nor used. Private-manifest activation follows offline\nvalidation of the new family.\n\nInspection of the actual management verifier found that its credential probe\nreads one latest security-profile entry (`limit=1`, `latest=true`) and discards\nthe response contents. It does not merely obtain a token. The owner explicitly\napproved this single-profile probe, retaining only verification status and call\nmetadata, within the two-read maximum and with no other inventory browsing or\nchanges. The earlier wording above must not be used to imply that it is token-only.\nThe exact bounded operation and input restrictions are now documented under\nL19 in `docs/planning/live-checks.md` and validated by `xtask::live`.\n\nThe offline regression first failed because L19 was an unknown family; it now\naccepts an optional complete designation and rejects scope expansion. This is\ntooling preparation, not a live receipt. The historical `live/blocked.json`\nremains unchanged until an approved actual wizard verification has a separate\nsource-bound receipt.\n{\n  \"schema\": \"airs-v2/l19-additional-grant/1\",\n  \"owner_approval\": \"Compare, refresh if different, allow 1 more probe\",\n  \"recorded_utc\": \"2026-11-01T13:36:31.023213+00:00\",\n  \"condition\": \"local secret differed; named reference corrected and verified\",\n  \"correction_record_sha256\": \"32fa5ff6634794e195a61f2cd86bcfee2be542251447eccf67233aeb045a7350\",\n  \"previous_manifest_sha256\": \"999f95abf2f6fb75f3597c95d7903a385eb7a1e876b99f6d63185378ba24499e\",\n  \"previous_read_reservations\": 2,\n  \"previous_ledger_sha256\": \"45d0456aef4d907dfadfcdf0475ff8126d024d9dfb0e38ab1dc097994fbcd945\",\n  \"new_manifest_sha256\": \"a2dd7b01ed289ed164859ac0daf6e582100de555d29eefb01fa13df87d0bdbe1\",\n  \"additional_read_cap\": 1,\n  \"maximum_cumulative_read_reservations\": 3,\n  \"previous_reservations_refunded\": 0,\n  \"operation\": \"same single latest-profile probe (limit=1), no other inventories or writes\"\n}\n{\n  \"valid\": true,\n  \"manifest_sha256\": \"a2dd7b01ed289ed164859ac0daf6e582100de555d29eefb01fa13df87d0bdbe1\",\n  \"activated_utc\": \"2026-11-01T13:37:53.919960+00:00\",\n  \"previous_read_reservations_preserved\": 2,\n  \"additional_read_cap\": 1,\n  \"validation_log_sha256\": \"281a69f81d8d2441559773e8e43d6416b8f2ccd1e9f49e096f4931a265f425ca\"\n}\n83:## Optional C29 wizard family L19\n85:L19 is a separately designated, read-only wizard qualification on Vulture\n88:L19 is reported as blocked, never inferred from L18's scan permission.\n92:It is not a token-only check. The explicit L19 operation is:\n94:> one management credential verification through the first-run wizard (C29): one latest security-profile probe with limit=1; discard profile contents; no other inventory browsing or writes\n96:L19 requires one `client_secret` Keychain reference, nonsecret `client_id`,\n100:Runtime Security in the wizard; its scan-key check is local storage validation,\n106:the source/build/manifest hashes, wizard verification status, nonsecret client\ntools/native-acceptance/test_live_c29_l19.py:15:        pending = json.loads((root / 'docs/planning/evidence/C29/live/L19/attempt-01/wizard-verify.json').read_text())\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:1://! L19 belongs to the real wizard, never the general C25 live runner.\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:8:fn wizard_only() -> serde_json::Value {\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:12:        \"L19\",\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:15:            \"credentials\": {\"client_secret\": super::common::keychain(\"wizard-not-resolved\")},\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:16:            \"nonsecret\": {\"client_id\": \"wizard@example.test\", \"tsg_id\": \"1852583913\", \"region\": \"us\"},\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:25:async fn an_optional_wizard_designation_never_enters_default_c25_execution() {\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:27:        .run(wizard_only(), &[], &secrets(&[]), Browser::idle())\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:29:    let record = result.expect(\"L19 must not be dispatched by the default C25 run\");\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:36:        .run(wizard_only(), &[\"L19\"], &secrets(&[]), Browser::idle())\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:38:    let error = result.expect_err(\"L19 requires the native first-run wizard\");\ncrates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs:42:            .contains(\"L19 requires the native first-run wizard\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'bundle_sha256|fn .*tree|fn hash_tree|fn tree_hash' crates/xtask/src; cat docs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-03/correction.diff docs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-04/relocation-proof.json; cat tools/native-acceptance/ax.swift\"","aggregated_output":"crates/xtask/src/shared.rs:100:fn verify_tree(root: &Path, dir: &Path) -> Result<()> {\ncrates/xtask/src/shared.rs:179:fn copy_tree(from: &Path, to: &Path) -> Result<()> {\ncrates/xtask/src/complete.rs:380:            prepared_bundle_sha256: prepared.as_ref().map(|p| p.bundle_sha256.clone()),\ncrates/xtask/src/complete.rs:383:            current_bundle_sha256: current.as_ref().and_then(|c| c.bundle_sha256.clone()),\ncrates/xtask/src/gate.rs:480:                if bundle.is_none() || bundle != native.prepared_bundle_sha256 {\ncrates/xtask/src/gate.rs:579:        prepared_bundle_sha256: base.prepared_bundle_sha256,\ncrates/xtask/src/gate.rs:582:        current_bundle_sha256: base.current_bundle_sha256,\ncrates/xtask/src/gate.rs:611:    pub prepared_bundle_sha256: Option<String>,\ncrates/xtask/src/gate.rs:614:    pub current_bundle_sha256: Option<String>,\ncrates/xtask/src/gate.rs:988:                    prepared_bundle_sha256: Some(BUNDLE_SHA.to_owned()),\ncrates/xtask/src/gate.rs:991:                    current_bundle_sha256: Some(BUNDLE_SHA.to_owned()),\ncrates/xtask/src/evidence.rs:97:            &expect.prepared_bundle_sha256,\ncrates/xtask/src/evidence.rs:98:            &expect.current_bundle_sha256,\ncrates/xtask/src/evidence.rs:165:    pub prepared_bundle_sha256: Option<String>,\ncrates/xtask/src/evidence.rs:169:    pub current_bundle_sha256: Option<String>,\ncrates/xtask/src/fingerprint.rs:133:pub fn tree_hash(dir: &Path) -> Result<String> {\ncrates/xtask/src/fingerprint.rs:138:pub fn tree_hash_excluding(dir: &Path, skip: &[&str]) -> Result<String> {\ncrates/xtask/src/fingerprint.rs:145:fn collect_tree(root: &Path, dir: &Path, skip: &[&str], out: &mut Vec<FileEntry>) -> Result<()> {\ncrates/xtask/src/native.rs:27:    pub bundle_sha256: String,\ncrates/xtask/src/native.rs:141:        bundle_sha256: fingerprint::tree_hash(&bundle)?,\ncrates/xtask/src/native.rs:160:    pub bundle_sha256: Option<String>,\ncrates/xtask/src/native.rs:170:        bundle_sha256: bundle\ncrates/xtask/src/native.rs:190:            sha256: prepared.bundle_sha256,\ncrates/xtask/src/native.rs:250:        prepared_bundle_sha256: prepared.as_ref().map(|p| p.bundle_sha256.clone()),\ncrates/xtask/src/native.rs:253:        current_bundle_sha256: current.as_ref().and_then(|c| c.bundle_sha256.clone()),\ncat: docs/planning/evidence/P09/check-remediation/attempt-03/correction.diff: No such file or directory\n{\n  \"fixture_impl_identical\": true,\n  \"remaining_source_identical\": true,\n  \"fixture_impl_sha256\": \"541c8f77605c48b546a0f42391592277f95361b054c8e3fa630ccba7e357ec95\",\n  \"comparison\": \"Remove exact original fixture-only trailing impl block from both sources and trim file trailing whitespace; all remaining bytes match. No production/test definitions changed.\"\n}\n// Minimal macOS Accessibility helper for native acceptance (compiled once\n// by the acceptance script with swiftc). It reads the real window's AX tree\n// and performs AX actions; keystrokes are sent separately through System\n// Events so input arrives as real keyboard events.\n//\n// Usage:\n//   ax tree  <pid>                          JSON list of nodes in the app's windows\n//   ax press <pid> <role> <label> [nth]     AXPress the nth matching element\n//   ax focus <pid> <role> <label> [nth]     set AXFocused on the nth match\n//   ax raise <pid>                          raise the main window\n//   ax type-file <pid> <file> [units]       type the file's text into the focused\n//                                           field as key events posted to <pid>,\n//                                           [units] UTF-16 units per event\n//                                           (default 20; up to 30000 pastes)\n// A node matches when its role equals <role> and its label (title,\n// description or string value) starts with <label>. Secure text fields\n// report the value the OS exposes for them (so evidence can show the key is\n// not exposed).\n\nimport AppKit\nimport ApplicationServices\nimport Foundation\n\nfunc attr(_ el: AXUIElement, _ name: String) -> AnyObject? {\n    var value: AnyObject?\n    return AXUIElementCopyAttributeValue(el, name as CFString, &value) == .success ? value : nil\n}\n\nfunc string(_ el: AXUIElement, _ name: String) -> String? {\n    attr(el, name) as? String\n}\n\nfunc point(_ el: AXUIElement) -> [Double]? {\n    guard let raw = attr(el, kAXPositionAttribute) else { return nil }\n    var p = CGPoint.zero\n    guard AXValueGetValue(raw as! AXValue, .cgPoint, &p) else { return nil }\n    return [Double(p.x), Double(p.y)]\n}\n\nfunc size(_ el: AXUIElement) -> [Double]? {\n    guard let raw = attr(el, kAXSizeAttribute) else { return nil }\n    var s = CGSize.zero\n    guard AXValueGetValue(raw as! AXValue, .cgSize, &s) else { return nil }\n    return [Double(s.width), Double(s.height)]\n}\n\nfunc children(_ el: AXUIElement) -> [AXUIElement] {\n    (attr(el, kAXChildrenAttribute) as? [AXUIElement]) ?? []\n}\n\nfunc label(_ el: AXUIElement) -> String {\n    for name in [kAXTitleAttribute, kAXDescriptionAttribute] {\n        if let s = string(el, name), !s.isEmpty { return s }\n    }\n    if let s = string(el, kAXValueAttribute) { return s }\n    return \"\"\n}\n\nstruct Node {\n    let el: AXUIElement\n    let depth: Int\n}\n\nfunc walk(_ pid: pid_t) -> [Node] {\n    let app = AXUIElementCreateApplication(pid)\n    // WebKit builds a web page's accessibility tree only for an AX client\n    // that announces itself (as assistive technologies do).\n    AXUIElementSetAttributeValue(app, \"AXEnhancedUserInterface\" as CFString, kCFBooleanTrue)\n    var out: [Node] = []\n    func visit(_ el: AXUIElement, _ depth: Int, panel: Bool = false) {\n        if out.count > 20000 || depth > 60 { return }\n        out.append(Node(el: el, depth: depth))\n        // Native file panels contain remote folder browsers. Describing their\n        // rows can stall AX for minutes and reads unrelated operator filenames.\n        // Keep actual panel controls (including nested Go to Folder sheets),\n        // with their roles, depths, geometry and focus. WebView trees retain\n        // their full traversal whenever no native sheet is present.\n        if panel && string(el, kAXRoleAttribute) == \"AXScrollArea\" { return }\n        for child in children(el) { visit(child, depth + 1, panel: panel) }\n    }\n    for window in (attr(app, kAXWindowsAttribute) as? [AXUIElement]) ?? [] {\n        let sheets = children(window).filter { string($0, kAXRoleAttribute) == \"AXSheet\" }\n        if sheets.isEmpty {\n            visit(window, 0)\n        } else {\n            out.append(Node(el: window, depth: 0))\n            for sheet in sheets { visit(sheet, 1, panel: true) }\n        }\n    }\n    return out\n}\n\nfunc describe(_ node: Node) -> [String: Any] {\n    let el = node.el\n    var d: [String: Any] = [\"depth\": node.depth]\n    d[\"role\"] = string(el, kAXRoleAttribute) ?? NSNull()\n    d[\"subrole\"] = string(el, kAXSubroleAttribute) ?? NSNull()\n    d[\"label\"] = label(el)\n    d[\"title\"] = string(el, kAXTitleAttribute) ?? NSNull()\n    d[\"description\"] = string(el, kAXDescriptionAttribute) ?? NSNull()\n    if let value = attr(el, kAXValueAttribute) {\n        if let s = value as? String { d[\"value\"] = s }\n        else if let n = value as? NSNumber { d[\"value\"] = n }\n    }\n    d[\"focused\"] = (attr(el, kAXFocusedAttribute) as? Bool) ?? false\n    d[\"enabled\"] = (attr(el, kAXEnabledAttribute) as? Bool) ?? true\n    d[\"current\"] = string(el, \"AXARIACurrent\") ?? NSNull()\n    if let url = attr(el, kAXURLAttribute) as? URL { d[\"url\"] = url.absoluteString }\n    d[\"pos\"] = point(el) ?? NSNull()\n    d[\"size\"] = size(el) ?? NSNull()\n    return d\n}\n\nfunc matches(_ pid: pid_t, _ role: String, _ prefix: String) -> [AXUIElement] {\n    walk(pid).map(\\.el).filter { string($0, kAXRoleAttribute) == role && label($0).hasPrefix(prefix) }\n}\n\nfunc fail(_ message: String) -> Never {\n    FileHandle.standardError.write((message + \"\\n\").data(using: .utf8)!)\n    exit(1)\n}\n\nlet args = CommandLine.arguments\nguard args.count >= 3, let pid = pid_t(args[2]) else { fail(\"usage: ax tree|press|focus|raise <pid> ...\") }\nswitch args[1] {\ncase \"tree\":\n    let nodes = walk(pid).map(describe)\n    let data = try! JSONSerialization.data(withJSONObject: nodes, options: [])\n    FileHandle.standardOutput.write(data)\ncase \"press\", \"focus\":\n    guard args.count >= 5 else { fail(\"\\(args[1]) needs <role> <label>\") }\n    let nth = args.count >= 6 ? Int(args[5]) ?? 0 : 0\n    let found = matches(pid, args[3], args[4])\n    guard nth < found.count else { fail(\"no \\(args[3]) labelled \\(args[4]) (\\(found.count) found)\") }\n    let el = found[nth]\n    let status = args[1] == \"press\"\n        ? AXUIElementPerformAction(el, kAXPressAction as CFString)\n        : AXUIElementSetAttributeValue(el, kAXFocusedAttribute as CFString, kCFBooleanTrue)\n    guard status == .success else { fail(\"\\(args[1]) failed: \\(status.rawValue)\") }\n    print(\"ok\")\ncase \"type-file\":\n    // Real keyboard events posted to this process only (CGEventPostToPid, so\n    // they can reach no other application), each carrying up to 20 UTF-16\n    // units of the file's text into the focused field. Used for inputs too\n    // large to type through System Events; the caller confirms the app is\n    // frontmost and verifies what arrived.\n    guard args.count >= 4, let text = try? String(contentsOfFile: args[3], encoding: .utf8) else { fail(\"type-file needs <file> [units per event]\") }\n    // 20 UTF-16 units per event mimics fast typing; larger events (WebKit\n    // truncates one event at 36,864 units) insert like a paste.\n    let perEvent = args.count >= 5 ? Int(args[4]) ?? 20 : 20\n    let source = CGEventSource(stateID: .hidSystemState)\n    var chunk: [UniChar] = []\n    func post(_ units: [UniChar]) {\n        guard let down = CGEvent(keyboardEventSource: source, virtualKey: 0, keyDown: true),\n              let up = CGEvent(keyboardEventSource: source, virtualKey: 0, keyDown: false) else { fail(\"cannot create key events\") }\n        units.withUnsafeBufferPointer { down.keyboardSetUnicodeString(stringLength: units.count, unicodeString: $0.baseAddress) }\n        down.postToPid(pid)\n        up.postToPid(pid)\n        // Large (paste-like) events get time to be applied before the next.\n        usleep(units.count > 20 ? 500_000 : 1_000)\n    }\n    for character in text {\n        let units = Array(String(character).utf16)\n        if chunk.count + units.count > perEvent { post(chunk); chunk = [] }\n        chunk.append(contentsOf: units)\n    }\n    if !chunk.isEmpty { post(chunk) }\n    print(\"ok\")\ncase \"raise\":\n    let app = AXUIElementCreateApplication(pid)\n    if let window = (attr(app, kAXWindowsAttribute) as? [AXUIElement])?.first {\n        AXUIElementPerformAction(window, kAXRaiseAction as CFString)\n    }\n    NSRunningApplication(processIdentifier: pid)?.activate()\n    print(\"ok\")\ndefault:\n    fail(\"unknown command \\(args[1])\")\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' tools/native-acceptance/live_c29_l19.py; cat tools/native-acceptance/test_live_c29_l19.py; cat crates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' tools/native-acceptance/live_c29_l19.py; cat tools/native-acceptance/test_live_c29_l19.py; cat crates/xtask/tests/live_run/wizard.rs\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"One approved C29 wizard verify. Run from the granted native queue, never\nagainst a synthetic-keychain fixture bundle. No automatic live retry.\n\nThe qualification bundle uses production adapters with a separate data identity;\nthe exact build, source, flags and executable are recorded by its build receipt.\nOnly a locally stored placeholder scan key and the approved management client\nare entered. Only Runtime Security is selected, and onboarding is not completed.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport datetime\nimport fcntl\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport fixture_app as fx\n\nIDENTITY = 'io.cdot.prisma-airs-desktop.v2.l19qual'\nSERVICE = 'io.cdot.prisma-airs-desktop.v2.scan'\nLIVE_REF = ('io.cdot.prisma-airs-desktop.v2.live', 'mgmt-vulture-client-secret')\nOPERATION = 'one management credential verification through the first-run wizard (C29): one latest security-profile probe with limit=1; discard profile contents; no other inventory browsing or writes'\nROOT = Path.cwd().resolve()\nDATA = Path.home() / 'Library/Application Support' / IDENTITY\nEXE = None\n\n\ndef sha(path):\n    return hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef write(path, value):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(value, indent=2) + '\\n')\n\n\nclass PrivateApp(fx.App):\n    @staticmethod\n    def running_pid():\n        rows = fx.sh(['ps', '-axo', 'pid=,comm=']).stdout.splitlines()\n        ids = [int(parts[0]) for row in rows if len(parts := row.strip().split(None, 1)) == 2 and parts[1] == str(EXE)]\n        if len(ids) > 1:\n            raise RuntimeError('multiple qualification processes')\n        return ids[0] if ids else None\n\n    def quit(self):\n        pid = self.running_pid()\n        if pid:\n            os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)\n            for _ in range(40):\n                if not self.running_pid():\n                    break\n                time.sleep(.25)\n            if self.running_pid():\n                os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n                time.sleep(.5)\n            if self.running_pid():\n                raise RuntimeError('qualification process did not stop')\n        self.pid = None\n\n    def ax(self, command, *args):\n        # No automatic diagnostic tree during private entry or on failure.\n        out = fx.sh([self.ax_bin, command, str(self.pid), *map(str, args)])\n        if out.returncode:\n            raise RuntimeError(f'accessibility {command} failed')\n        return json.loads(out.stdout or '[]') if command == 'tree' else out.stdout\n\n    def private_type(self, label, value, helper):\n        self.ax('focus', 'AXTextField', label, 0)\n        self.front()\n        result = subprocess.run([str(helper), str(self.pid)], input=value, text=True, capture_output=True)\n        if result.returncode:\n            raise RuntimeError('private credential entry failed')\n        time.sleep(.5)\n        field = self.field('AXTextField', label) or {}\n        arrived = str(field.get('value') or '')\n        if len(arrived) != len(value) or not set(arrived) <= {'•'}:\n            raise RuntimeError('private field did not report a masked value')\n\n\ndef require(app, predicate, message, timeout=20):\n    tree, ok = app.wait_for(predicate, timeout)\n    if not ok:\n        raise RuntimeError(message)\n    return tree\n\n\ndef press(app, label):\n    require(app, lambda t: app.node(t, 'AXButton', label) is not None, f'{label} unavailable')\n    app.ax('press', 'AXButton', label)\n    time.sleep(.5)\n\n\ndef verify_finished(tree):\n    terminal = {\n        'Checks finished; nothing failed.',\n        'Checks finished with warnings.',\n        'A required check failed.',\n        'An optional check failed. You can fix it and verify again, or continue with it recorded as a warning.',\n    }\n    labels = {n.get('label') for n in tree if n.get('role') in ('AXStaticText', 'AXHeading')}\n    return bool(labels & terminal) and 'Checking…' not in labels\n\n\ndef reserve_read(path, manifest_sha, attempt, limit):\n    \"\"\"Append a conservative reservation before admission; never refund one.\"\"\"\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o600)\n    with os.fdopen(fd, 'a+', encoding='utf-8') as ledger:\n        fcntl.flock(ledger, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        assert os.fstat(ledger.fileno()).st_mode & 0o077 == 0, 'budget ledger must be private'\n        ledger.seek(0)\n        raw = ledger.read()\n        entries = [json.loads(line) for line in raw.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n        assert all(e['manifest_sha256'] == manifest_sha for e in entries), 'budget manifest changed'\n        assert not any(e['attempt'] == attempt for e in entries), 'attempt already reserved'\n        used = sum(e['reads_reserved'] for e in entries)\n        assert all(e['reads_reserved'] == 1 for e in entries) and used < limit <= 2, 'read budget exhausted'\n        ledger.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)\n        if raw and not raw.endswith('\\n'):\n            ledger.write('\\n')\n        ledger.write(json.dumps({'manifest_sha256': manifest_sha, 'attempt': attempt, 'reads_reserved': 1}) + '\\n')\n        ledger.flush()\n        os.fsync(ledger.fileno())\n    return used + 1\n\n\ndef credential_ids():\n    path = DATA / 'state.json'\n    if not path.exists():\n        return set()\n    state = json.loads(path.read_text())\n    return {c['record'] for c in state.get('credentials', [])} | set(state.get('pendingCleanup', []))\n\n\ndef main():\n    global EXE\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--scope', required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument('--build', required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument('--validated', required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument('--budget-ledger', required=True, type=Path)\n    parser.add_argument('--attempt', required=True)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    assert re.fullmatch(r'attempt-\\d{2}', args.attempt)\n    scope_bytes = args.scope.read_bytes()\n    scope_sha = hashlib.sha256(scope_bytes).hexdigest()\n    scope = json.loads(scope_bytes)\n    validated = json.loads(args.validated.read_text())\n    assert validated['manifest_sha256'] == scope_sha and validated['valid'] is True\n    family = scope['families']['L19']\n    assert family['status'] == 'designated' and family['environment'] == 'test-b'\n    assert family['permitted_operations'] == [OPERATION]\n    assert family['budget'] in ({'reads': 1}, {'reads': 2})\n    assert family['nonsecret']['tsg_id'] == '1852583913' and family['nonsecret']['region'] == 'us'\n    ref = family['credentials']['client_secret']\n    assert ref['kind'] == 'keychain' and (ref['service'], ref['account']) == LIVE_REF\n    build = json.loads(args.build.read_text())\n    assert Path(build['source_root']).resolve() == ROOT\n    assert build['identifier'] == IDENTITY and build['features'] == []\n    inventory = ROOT / build['source_inventory']\n    assert sha(inventory) == build['source_inputs_sha256']\n    for line in inventory.read_text().splitlines():\n        expected, relative = line.split(None, 1)\n        assert sha(ROOT / relative.lstrip(' *')) == expected, 'qualification source changed after build'\n    bundle = Path(build['bundle'])\n    EXE = bundle / 'Contents/MacOS/prisma-airs-desktop-v2'\n    assert sha(EXE) == build['executable_sha256']\n    actual_id = fx.sh(['plutil', '-extract', 'CFBundleIdentifier', 'raw', '-o', '-', str(bundle / 'Contents/Info.plist')]).stdout.strip()\n    assert actual_id == IDENTITY\n    assert not DATA.exists(), 'qualification data root must be fresh'\n    out = ROOT / 'docs/planning/evidence/C29/live/L19' / args.attempt\n    assert not out.exists(), 'never overwrite an earlier live attempt'\n    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n    work = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='airs-l19-'))\n    work.chmod(0o700)\n    helper = work / 'private-input'\n    compiled = fx.sh(['swiftc', '-O', str(Path(__file__).with_name('type_private_stdin.swift')), '-o', str(helper)])\n    assert compiled.returncode == 0, 'private input helper failed to compile'\n    app = PrivateApp(str(bundle), str(work), [])\n    receipt = {'schema': 'airs-v2/live-row/1', 'subject': 'C29', 'family': 'L19',\n               'performed_by': 'Codex through the granted Kitty native queue',\n               'attempt': args.attempt, 'status': 'failed', 'recorded_utc': datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n               'manifest_sha256': scope_sha, 'build_receipt_sha256': sha(args.build),\n               'executable_sha256': build['executable_sha256'], 'source_inputs_sha256': build['source_inputs_sha256'],\n               'client_id': family['nonsecret']['client_id'], 'tsg_id': '1852583913',\n               'operation': OPERATION, 'wizard_verify_intents': 0, 'read_budget_reserved': 0,\n               'http_requests_observed': False, 'automatic_retries': 0, 'products': ['runtimeSecurity'],\n               'evidence': [], 'local_credentials_removed': False,\n               'limitations': ['Request bound comes from the inspected production verifier (limit=1, latest=true, SDK retries=0) and exactly one wizard intent; no TLS interception or response body capture.']}\n    write(out / 'build.json', build)\n    shutil.copy2(inventory, out / 'source-inputs.sha256')\n    ids = set()\n    secret = ''\n    stage = 'launch'\n    try:\n        app.launch()\n        stage = 'create draft'\n        press(app, 'Set up a tenant')\n        app.type_into('AXTextField', 'Display name', 'Vulture L19 qualification')\n        app.type_into('AXTextField', 'TSG ID', '1852583913')\n        app.ax('press', 'AXRadioButton', 'Other')\n        press(app, 'Create tenant')\n        require(app, lambda t: app.node(t, 'AXButton', 'Save scan key') is not None, 'draft unavailable')\n        app.private_type('Scan API key', 'l19-local-placeholder-never-sent', helper)\n        press(app, 'Save scan key')\n        require(app, lambda t: app.node(t, 'AXButton', 'Replace scan key') is not None, 'scan placeholder not stored')\n        ids |= credential_ids()\n        stage = 'store management client'\n        app.type_into('AXTextField', 'Client ID', family['nonsecret']['client_id'])\n        resolved = subprocess.run(['security', 'find-generic-password', '-w', '-s', ref['service'], '-a', ref['account']], capture_output=True)\n\"\"\"Offline regressions for live-driver admission; never resolve credentials.\"\"\"\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport live_c29_l19 as driver\n\n\nclass Settlement(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_the_actual_pending_tree_is_not_a_finished_verification(self):\n        root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n        pending = json.loads((root / 'docs/planning/evidence/C29/live/L19/attempt-01/wizard-verify.json').read_text())\n        self.assertTrue(any(n.get('label') == 'Pending' for n in pending))\n        self.assertFalse(driver.verify_finished(pending))\n\n    def test_terminal_success_and_failure_are_finished_but_reading_is_not(self):\n        for label in ['Checks finished; nothing failed.', 'Checks finished with warnings.', 'A required check failed.', 'An optional check failed. You can fix it and verify again, or continue with it recorded as a warning.']:\n            tree = [{'role': 'AXStaticText', 'label': label}]\n            self.assertTrue(driver.verify_finished(tree))\n            self.assertFalse(driver.verify_finished(tree + [{'role': 'AXStaticText', 'label': 'Checking…'}]))\n\n\nclass Budget(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_interrupted_first_attempt_stays_charged_and_a_third_is_refused(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n            path = Path(directory) / 'ledger.jsonl'\n            self.assertEqual(driver.reserve_read(path, 'scope', 'attempt-01', 2), 1)\n            self.assertEqual(driver.reserve_read(path, 'scope', 'attempt-02', 2), 2)\n            before = path.read_bytes()\n            with self.assertRaises(AssertionError):\n                driver.reserve_read(path, 'scope', 'attempt-03', 2)\n            self.assertEqual(path.read_bytes(), before)\n\n    def test_duplicate_attempt_changed_scope_and_one_read_cap_refuse(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n            path = Path(directory) / 'ledger.jsonl'\n            driver.reserve_read(path, 'scope', 'attempt-01', 1)\n            for scope, attempt, limit in [('scope', 'attempt-01', 2), ('other', 'attempt-02', 2), ('scope', 'attempt-02', 1)]:\n                with self.assertRaises(AssertionError):\n                    driver.reserve_read(path, scope, attempt, limit)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\n//! L19 belongs to the real wizard, never the general C25 live runner.\n\nuse serde_json::json;\nuse xtask::live;\n\nuse super::common::{Browser, Fixture, designate, manifest, secrets};\n\nfn wizard_only() -> serde_json::Value {\n    let mut value = manifest();\n    designate(\n        &mut value,\n        \"L19\",\n        json!({\n            \"environment\": \"test-b\",\n            \"credentials\": {\"client_secret\": super::common::keychain(\"wizard-not-resolved\")},\n            \"nonsecret\": {\"client_id\": \"wizard@example.test\", \"tsg_id\": \"1852583913\", \"region\": \"us\"},\n            \"permitted_operations\": [live::WIZARD_VERIFY_OPERATION],\n            \"budget\": {\"reads\": 2}\n        }),\n    );\n    value\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn an_optional_wizard_designation_never_enters_default_c25_execution() {\n    let (_, result) = Fixture::new()\n        .run(wizard_only(), &[], &secrets(&[]), Browser::idle())\n        .await;\n    let record = result.expect(\"L19 must not be dispatched by the default C25 run\");\n    assert!(record.families.is_empty());\n}\n\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn explicitly_selecting_l19_refuses_before_resolving_its_secret() {\n    let (_, result) = Fixture::new()\n        .run(wizard_only(), &[\"L19\"], &secrets(&[]), Browser::idle())\n        .await;\n    let error = result.expect_err(\"L19 requires the native first-run wizard\");\n    assert!(\n        error\n            .to_string()\n            .contains(\"L19 requires the native first-run wizard\")\n    );\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
